l Media Manager"],"job_types":["Werkstudent","working student","hilfstätigkeit / student"],"location":"Hofheim","created_at":1794411077},{"slug":"working-student-b2g-public-sector-research-funding-munster-499167","company_name":"RIZM","title":"Working Student B2G: Public Sector & Research Funding (f/m/d)","description":"<h2>01 · Why this role exists</h2><p><strong>This is not your typical student job.</strong></p><p>B2G sounds boring, until you realise it's money from the state and you help win it. You'll work directly with our B2G Manager and the founders on funding that flows straight into RIZM's cash flow, and you'll see from the inside how the public sector decides and buys. Something most students never get to see.</p><p>RIZM builds RIZMO, an AI agent that makes energy decisions for industrial companies. Our next lever is the public sector: municipalities, utilities and economic development agencies have to implement heat plans, keep business parks competitive and relieve the grid. We're building B2G as a new business line at RIZM, and we're looking for a working student to help build it from day one.</p><h2>02 · What you'll do</h2><ul><li><p><strong>Public funding as a growth channel:</strong> Help build the pipeline for Forschungszulage (Germany's R&D tax allowance), EU grants, ERDF (EFRE) and other programmes: scout new calls, prepare applications and keep track of our running programmes.</p></li><li><p><strong>Connect research:</strong> Support our research collaboration with Stanford and help turn it into funded projects.</p></li><li><p><strong>Build the machine, AI-first:</strong> Set up trackers, automations and AI workflows so our funding pipeline runs with as little manual work as possible. Your ideas count here.</p></li><li><p><strong>Support ReNET-EV:</strong> Help with our part of the ERDF project ReNET-EV (grid-friendly energy supply for business parks in the Münster/NRW region): documentation, reporting and the rollout to more municipalities.</p><