m that enables engineering teams to build and run AI-powered software factories, where coding agents take on real development work, from picking up engineering tickets to implementing changes and creating pull requests.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">By combining structured context, reusable agent skills, automated workflows and evaluations, we're making AI-powered development more reliable, repeatable and scalable, while keeping humans in control. We're tackling some of the biggest challenges in autonomous software development, from code quality and security to helping organisations confidently adopt AI agents at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded by Guy Podjarny, previously founder of Snyk, Tessl is a fast-growing Series A startup backed by over $100 million in funding from investors including Index Ventures, Accel, GV and Boldstart.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Joining Tessl means helping define an entirely new category of technology, solving ambitious technical challenges and shaping the future of software development.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>ABOUT THE ROLE</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re hiring a Demand Generation Manager to build and scale Tessl’s growth engine.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll own pipeline creation across channels — from experimentation to execution. This is a hands-on, data-driven individual contributor role focused on building repeatable, measurable demand in a developer-first market.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll work closely with Product Marketing, Content, and Sales to ensure we’re attracting the right audiences and converting attention into high-quality pipeline.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you love testing hypotheses, building systems from scratch, and turning signal into scalable growth, this role is for you..</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>WHAT YOU'LL DO</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pipeline Strategy &amp; Execution</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own demand generation strategy across paid, organic, partnerships, and community channels</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and optimise multi-channel campaigns aligned to product launches and GTM priorities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive MQL → SQL pipeline growth with clear attribution and reporting</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experimentation &amp; Optimisation</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run rapid growth experiments across paid media, landing pages, email, and content distribution</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage budget allocation across channels based on performance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve conversion rates across the funnel</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Performance &amp; Analytics</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and track core growth metrics (CAC, CPL, conversion rates, pipeline contribution)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build dashboards and reporting frameworks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use data to continuously refine strategy</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-Functional Collaboration</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Product Marketing on launch amplification</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Align with Sales on ICP targeting and pipeline quality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with Content to maximise distribution and reach</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>WHAT WE'RE LOOKING FOR</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Must have:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">4–8+ years in demand generation or growth marketing (B2B SaaS preferred)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience owning paid acquisition and multi-channel campaigns</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical skills and comfort with attribution models</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated success building pipeline in early-stage or high-growth environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bias for action and experimentation mindset</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience marketing to developers or technical audiences</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with PLG + sales-assisted hybrid funnels</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with marketing automation and CRM tooling (e.g. HubSpot, Salesforce)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Application Process</strong></h2><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Introductory call</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hiring manager interview</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical growth case discussion</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cross-functional interviews</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final conversation with leadership</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Life at Tessl</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We want Tessl to be a place where you can do meaningful work, keep learning and enjoy being part of the team. Alongside competitive compensation, we offer benefits designed to support you both inside and outside work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive compensation and equity:</strong> Market-benchmarked salaries and EMI share options.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Time off:</strong> 25 days of annual leave, plus UK public holidays, and two paid volunteering days each year.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Private healthcare:</strong> Vitality medical insurance, including dental, optical and mental health support, with cover included for partners and dependants.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pension:</strong> A 5% employer pension matched contribution through Smart Pension.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Life assurance:</strong> Company-paid life insurance with MetLife providing cover of four times your annual salary.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Family Leave:</strong> We offer enhanced Maternity, Parental and Adoption Leave from day one to support you and your growing family.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning and development:</strong> We support opportunities to continue developing your skills with a £1,000 per year to spend.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commuting benefits:</strong> Financial support for eligible team members commuting from outside Greater London, plus a Cycle to Work scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Summer &amp; winter offsites:</strong> Twice a year, we bring the whole Tessl team together for a week-long offsite. It's a chance to step away from our usual routines, collaborate on big ideas, build stronger relationships and enjoy shared experiences together. And of course, we have a lot of fun along the way!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Our London HQ</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our office is in the heart of King's Cross, surrounded by London's growing AI and technology community.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work together in person on Mondays, Tuesdays and Thursdays, giving us time to collaborate, exchange ideas and build relationships. You'll also enjoy catered lunches (Tuesday &amp; Thursday), plenty of office snacks, regular team lunches and socials, plus a pet-friendly workplace.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>How we work</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our operating principles shape how we collaborate and make decisions. We move quickly and learn by doing, build on ideas before challenging them, get stuck in wherever we can help, and give people real ownership. We encourage thoughtful debate, curiosity and a willingness to try things that haven't been done before. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://tessl.io/careers">Read our five operating principles</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>We're AI native</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI isn't just what we're building - it's central to how we work every day, across every function. We actively use AI to improve how we work, solve problems and challenge traditional ways of doing things.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don't need to be an AI expert to thrive at Tessl, but you do need curiosity, an appetite for experimentation and a willingness to embrace new ways of working. We expect everyone to use AI regularly, invest time in learning how to get the most from it and keep experimenting when something doesn't work the first time, rather than defaulting to manual approaches.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're also big believers in sharing what we learn. We encourage transparency about how we're using AI, what's working, what isn't and how we can help each other improve. Being AI native doesn't mean removing human judgement, it means using AI thoughtfully, while taking ownership of the quality and outcomes of our work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Everyone is welcome at Tessl</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're committed to building an inclusive environment where people from different backgrounds, experiences and perspectives can thrive.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We particularly welcome applications from people who are underrepresented in technology. If you're excited about the opportunity but don't meet every requirement, we'd still encourage you to apply.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you need any adjustments or additional support during the recruitment process, please let us know. We're happy to work with you to make the process accessible and comfortable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Come build with us</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're moving fast, experimenting boldly and figuring things out as we go. There's plenty to build, lots to learn and real opportunities to make your mark.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're excited by big ideas, enjoy getting stuck in and want to be part of something from the ground up, we'd love to hear from you!</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/tesslcareers/member-of-marketing-staff-marketing-manager-demand-generation-london-289775","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London Office","created_at":1794454816},{"slug":"member-of-technical-staff-platform-leaning-london-14977","company_name":"Tesslcareers","title":"Member of Technical Staff (Platform Leaning)","description":"<h1><strong>About Tessl</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI is transforming how software is built, and at Tessl, we're building the infrastructure for what comes next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're developing a platform that enables engineering teams to build and run AI-powered software factories, where coding agents take on real development work, from picking up engineering tickets to implementing changes and creating pull requests.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">By combining structured context, reusable agent skills, automated workflows and evaluations, we're making AI-powered development more reliable, repeatable and scalable, while keeping humans in control. We're tackling some of the biggest challenges in autonomous software development, from code quality and security to helping organisations confidently adopt AI agents at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded by Guy Podjarny, previously founder of Snyk, Tessl is a fast-growing Series A startup backed by over $100 million in funding from investors including Index Ventures, Accel, GV and Boldstart.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Joining Tessl means helping define an entirely new category of technology, solving ambitious technical challenges and shaping the future of software development.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>OVERVIEW OF THE ROLE</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join our engineering team to build real-time AI Native workflows, tooling, and interfaces that will reshape how developers create and maintain software.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a product engineering role with a platform twist. Most of your time, you'll do what every Tessl engineer does: design, prototype and ship product features end to end, collaborating closely with product, design and the wider engineering team in a fast-paced, high-autonomy environment. What makes you different is that when the work goes below the application layer, you light up rather than back away: complex networking scenarios such as site-to-site VPN and private connectivity, multi-cloud and multi-region deployments, observability, and the machinery that makes Tessl straightforward to deploy, operate and support wherever it needs to run.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We expect you to be relentlessly AI native about it: instead of triaging alerts at 2 am, you'll build or deploy the agent that does it. Instead of reacting to scaling bottlenecks, you'll create systems that spot them before they happen. Deep expertise is the foundation, because you can't automate what you don't know, but your ambition should be to make agents do the bulk of the operational work, with you supervising and steering.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're open on level for this role, from mid-level to senior: trajectory and appetite matter more to us than years.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What success looks like:</strong> Within your first year, you're shipping product features end to end like any Tessl engineer. When infrastructure work arises, from deployment architecture to networking to observability, you're the one who takes it on and lands it well, with support where you need it. Our deployment and operational practices are stronger because of you, agentic tooling handles a growing share of the toil, and the infrastructure work you touch is compliant by default, keeping our ISO 27001 and SOC 2 journey unblocked.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>WHAT YOU'LL DO</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">No two days will be the same at Tessl! You'll have a high level of autonomy and be empowered to make decisions based on what you believe will help you deliver the most success. Here's an insight into just a few of the things you would be doing:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product engineering (most of your time)</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and implement new functionality end to end, from initial design and prototypes to fully scoped production implementations, reviewed with the product team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rapidly prototype new capabilities to prove or disprove an idea, then develop a plan for a scalable implementation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pair with designers and other engineers to make the experience intuitive and slick, and integrate third-party services so we can focus our cycles on Tessl's core capabilities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gather requirements from customers and stakeholders, turn ambiguity into agreed plans, and deliver them</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Platform &amp; infrastructure</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lean into infrastructure work as it arises: our AWS estate (EKS/Kubernetes), infrastructure-as-code, CI/CD with GitHub Actions, and our observability stack (Dash0/OpenTelemetry, Sentry, PostHog)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to the architecture &amp; build of our more complex networking and deployment scenarios, such as private connectivity and multi-region setups</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve developer experience and platform ergonomics so every engineer at Tessl ships faster</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with our Infosec team so that everything you build is compliant by default, contributing infrastructure controls and evidence towards ISO 27001 and SOC 2</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-native automation</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build or deploy agentic tooling that picks up firing alerts and works through diagnostic steps autonomously, giving a human supervisor a detailed assessment with recommended actions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build agents that keep our estate healthy without human toil: dependency upgrades that test and merge themselves, alerts that arrive pre-diagnosed, runbooks that execute instead of sitting in a wiki</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continuously spot repetitive manual work, across product, platform and on-call workflows, and convert it into agent-driven automation</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>WHAT WE'RE LOOKING FOR</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for someone who is as excited as we are to be part of a dynamic team that is shaping the future of AI and software development. We're committed to building a diverse team and strongly encourage applications from people of all backgrounds, identities, and experiences.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Must-haves</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Proven experience as a Software Engineer</strong> (TypeScript/Node preferred): you care about code modularity, structure and aesthetics, and you're equally comfortable contributing to a mature codebase with strict CI criteria or hacking up a quick prototype to prove an assumption</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A genuine pull towards platform and infrastructure work</strong>, backed by hands-on experience: you've deployed and operated real systems (Kubernetes, cloud environments, infrastructure-as-code, CI/CD), and when the chance came to go deeper, you took it, whether that was owning platform or DevOps work in a previous role or picking up the infrastructure tasks nobody else wanted</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Solid systems and networking fundamentals</strong>: DNS, TLS, VPCs, firewalls; you can reason and debug below the application layer with confidence</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Demonstrated use of AI coding tools and agents</strong> to accelerate your own work, and excitement about experimenting with new AI approaches to transform how engineering is done</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Comfortable with fast-paced, high-autonomy environments</strong>: you turn loose requirements into plans and shipped work without waiting to be told</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice-to-haves</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You self-host things for fun</strong>: a homelab, your own services, a Kubernetes cluster nobody asked you to run</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Production AWS/EKS experience</strong>, or hands-on work with private connectivity, VPNs, or multi-region architectures</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience producing infrastructure evidence</strong> for certifications such as ISO 27001 or SOC 2</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You've thrived in an early-stage startup before</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Have a cool project to show us</strong> (GitHub links welcome!)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The kind of person you are</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're a product engineer first: you measure infrastructure by what it lets the team ship, and you see platform work as making every engineer faster, never a domain to guard</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're calm under pressure, including when production is misbehaving and the answer is three layers down the stack</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You think big about how AI changes the job: the best engineers automate themselves out of the repetitive loop and operate at the scale of a team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're comfortable with ambiguity and rapid change, and you grab a shovel when something needs doing outside your lane</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You communicate clearly and bring people along: product, security, engineers and customers all need to trust your judgement</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Application Process</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here's an outline of what you can expect during our interview process:</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Introductory Call</strong> with one of our engineering leaders. A relaxed chat to learn about your background, interests, and career goals. We'll also share more about the role, Tessl's vision, and answer any questions you have.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Take-Home Exercise.</strong> You'll receive a practical challenge based on real scenarios you might tackle at Tessl: an opportunity to showcase your approach to problem-solving on your own schedule.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>On-site Technical Session.</strong> You'll pair with two of our lead engineers to build on your take-home exercise. This session simulates working together on real problems and allows us to explore your technical expertise more deeply.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Culture Conversation</strong> with our People Lead. A two-way dialogue about our values, team dynamic, and your motivations. Feel free to ask about life at Tessl, growth opportunities, or anything else you're curious about.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Leadership Discussion</strong> with Maurilio (Head of Engineering), and potentially also with Guy (CEO) or Dru (Head of Product). Our final stage focuses on strategic alignment and long-term vision. You'll learn more about Tessl's roadmap and how you could contribute to our mission.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Throughout the process, if you have any specific requirements or need adjustments, please let us know: we're happy to accommodate.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Life at Tessl</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We want Tessl to be a place where you can do meaningful work, keep learning and enjoy being part of the team. Alongside competitive compensation, we offer benefits designed to support you both inside and outside work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive compensation and equity:</strong> Market-benchmarked salaries and EMI share options.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Time off:</strong> 25 days of annual leave, plus UK public holidays, and two paid volunteering days each year.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Private healthcare:</strong> Vitality medical insurance, including dental, optical and mental health support, with cover included for partners and dependants.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pension:</strong> A 5% employer pension matched contribution through Smart Pension.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Life assurance:</strong> Company-paid life insurance with MetLife providing cover of four times your annual salary.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Family Leave:</strong> We offer enhanced Maternity, Parental and Adoption Leave from day one to support you and your growing family.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning and development:</strong> We support opportunities to continue developing your skills with a £1,000 per year to spend.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commuting benefits:</strong> Financial support for eligible team members commuting from outside Greater London, plus a Cycle to Work scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Summer &amp; winter offsites:</strong> Twice a year, we bring the whole Tessl team together for a week-long offsite. It's a chance to step away from our usual routines, collaborate on big ideas, build stronger relationships and enjoy shared experiences together. And of course, we have a lot of fun along the way!</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Our London HQ</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our office is in the heart of King's Cross, surrounded by London's growing AI and technology community.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work together in person on Mondays, Tuesdays and Thursdays, giving us time to collaborate, exchange ideas and build relationships. You'll also enjoy catered lunches (Tuesday &amp; Thursday), plenty of office snacks, regular team lunches and socials, plus a pet-friendly workplace.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>How we work</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our operating principles shape how we collaborate and make decisions. We move quickly and learn by doing, build on ideas before challenging them, get stuck in wherever we can help, and give people real ownership. We encourage thoughtful debate, curiosity and a willingness to try things that haven't been done before. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://tessl.io/careers">Read our five operating principles</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>We're AI native</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI isn't just what we're building - it's central to how we work every day, across every function. We actively use AI to improve how we work, solve problems and challenge traditional ways of doing things.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don't need to be an AI expert to thrive at Tessl, but you do need curiosity, an appetite for experimentation and a willingness to embrace new ways of working. We expect everyone to use AI regularly, invest time in learning how to get the most from it and keep experimenting when something doesn't work the first time, rather than defaulting to manual approaches.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're also big believers in sharing what we learn. We encourage transparency about how we're using AI, what's working, what isn't and how we can help each other improve. Being AI native doesn't mean removing human judgement, it means using AI thoughtfully, while taking ownership of the quality and outcomes of our work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Everyone is welcome at Tessl</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're committed to building an inclusive environment where people from different backgrounds, experiences and perspectives can thrive.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We particularly welcome applications from people who are underrepresented in technology. If you're excited about the opportunity but don't meet every requirement, we'd still encourage you to apply.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you need any adjustments or additional support during the recruitment process, please let us know. We're happy to work with you to make the process accessible and comfortable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Come build with us</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're moving fast, experimenting boldly and figuring things out as we go. There's plenty to build, lots to learn and real opportunities to make your mark.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're excited by big ideas, enjoy getting stuck in and want to be part of something from the ground up, we'd love to hear from you!</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/tesslcareers/member-of-technical-staff-platform-leaning-london-14977","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London Office","created_at":1794454816},{"slug":"account-executive-defence-london-129496","company_name":"Applied","title":"Account Executive, Defence","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Applied Intuition, Inc. is powering the future of physical AI. Founded in 2017 and now valued at $15 billion, the Silicon Valley company is creating the digital infrastructure needed to bring intelligence to every moving machine on the planet. Applied Intuition services the automotive, defense, trucking, construction, mining and agriculture industries in three core areas: tools and infrastructure, operating systems, and autonomy. Eighteen of the top 20 global automakers, as well as the United States military and its allies, trust the company’s solutions to deliver physical intelligence. Applied Intuition is headquartered in Sunnyvale, California, with offices in Washington, D.C.; San Diego; Ft. Walton Beach, Florida; Ann Arbor, Michigan; London; Stuttgart; Munich; Stockholm; Bangalore; Seoul; and Tokyo. Learn more at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://applied.co">applied.co</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We are an in-office company, and our expectation is that full-time employees primarily work from their Applied Intuition office 5 days a week. However, we also recognize the importance of flexibility and trust our employees to manage their schedules responsibly. This may include occasional remote work, starting the day with morning meetings from home before heading to the office, or leaving earlier when needed to accommodate family commitments. This in-office expectation does not apply to contractor positions</em></p><h3><strong>About the role</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be the commercial lead for our major European partners and our UK Land programmes, and for new partner, prime and Land accounts across the UK and Europe. You will own these relationships, grow live pilots into multi-year programmes and partnerships, and coordinate our Growth, Solutions and Forward Deployed Engineering teams to deliver. You will be based in London and spend regular time with customers across the UK and with our partners in Europe.<br /></p><h3><strong>At Applied Intuition, you will:</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own relationships with our major partners and UK Land customers end to end: engagement cadence, stakeholder map across business units, and a clear account plan</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Grow live pilots into multi-year programmes and partnerships, shaping follow-on work across our Axion, Acuity and platform products</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate internal teams around active pursuits, keep pipeline and account plans current, and align customer and partner priorities with what we can deliver</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive continuity through award and delivery, manage escalations, and find follow-ons, renewals and adjacent programmes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Open new partner, prime and Land accounts across the UK and Europe, finding new budget lines, programmes and contacts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape the scope of technical deals with our Solutions Engineers rather than selling off a price sheet</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work within export-control, classification and data-sovereignty constraints in every engagement<br /></p></li></ul><h3><strong>We're looking for someone who has:</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of owning customer or partner relationships and driving deals to award in European defence, as an account executive, BD lead or ex-military acquisition or capability officer</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing and growing a strategic partner, prime or OEM relationship, or selling into UK Land programmes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A consultative, solution-selling approach and enough technical literacy to be credible with engineers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A live network across UK Land and European defence primes and programmes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong organisational discipline: account plans, meeting notes, follow-up tracking and CRM (Salesforce) hygiene</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High energy, a natural networking instinct, and comfort with ambiguity and rejection</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bachelor's degree or equivalent military experience</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Travel requirements</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regular travel to Europe and to customer sites across the UK.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Security requirements</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Must have the ability to obtain UK Security Clearance (SC)</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Nice to have</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">UK Land domain (British Army, DE&amp;S) or European defence industry experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience at a defence-tech start-up, autonomy company or prime</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of UK and European defence acquisition (MOD, DE&amp;S, FMV)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with structured sales qualification such as MEDDPICC</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Service in the UK or allied armed forces</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Don’t meet every single requirement? If you’re excited about this role but your past experience doesn’t align perfectly with every qualification in the job description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Applied Intuition is an equal opportunity employer and federal contractor or subcontractor. Consequently, the parties agree that, as applicable, they will abide by the requirements of 41 CFR 60-1.4(a), 41 CFR 60-300.5(a) and 41 CFR 60-741.5(a) and that these laws are incorporated herein by reference. These regulations prohibit discrimination against qualified individuals based on their status as protected veterans or individuals with disabilities, and prohibit discrimination against all individuals based on their race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or national origin. These regulations require that covered prime contractors and subcontractors take affirmative action to employ and advance in employment individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status or disability. The parties also agree that, as applicable, they will abide by the requirements of Executive Order 13496 (29 CFR Part 471, Appendix A to Subpart A), relating to the notice of employee rights under federal labor laws.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>FOR US-BASED ROLES: </strong><em>Applied Intuition is committed to providing an accessible and inclusive application and interview experience to applicants who are disabled veterans and other applicants with disabilities or medical conditions. Reasonable accommodations are available, requesting an accommodation will not affect your candidacy in any way, and you are not required to disclose the nature of your disability or medical condition in order to make a request. If you require an accommodation please contact </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" ---------- We will work with you!</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/applied/account-executive-defence-london-129496","tags":["Software Engineering - Defense"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794454816},{"slug":"senior-sales-engineer-focus-enterprise-united-kingdom-139528","company_name":"Sophos","title":"Senior Sales Engineer - Focus Enterprise","description":"<h2>The Opportunity</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Senior Field Sales Engineer drives Sophos’ growth by technically engaging with our existing enterprise customer base to broaden our presence in accounts as well as winning customers who have not previously adopted any of our technologies.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role requires skills and experience in the technical management of existing customers, building a trust relationship focused on driving the business benefits to be gained from the adoption of the Sophos solution set, together with the ability to drive new logo business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will have a demonstrably strong background in supporting the sale of security technologies including XDR/MDR, network security, and endpoint solutions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Alongside strong technical skills around the enterprise security stack, the role requires effective technical storytelling, and commercial appreciation in order to quickly establish trust from first contact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will work alongside nominated members of the sales team and members of our reseller partner network to develop the existing client base and drive new-logo opportunities. Key to your success in this role will be your ability to become a trusted business partner for your nominated sellers and other internal Sophos stakeholders e.g. Customer Success Managers, Product Managers, drive compelling technical value propositions into your customers and prospects.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead technical engagement for existing and net‑new prospects from first conversation through to technical win, focusing on competitive differentiation and value‑led positioning.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rapidly assess a prospect’s environment, risks, and security maturity to recommend impactful solutions that connect with their business objectives</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take ownership of those solutions including internal stakeholder management to bring appropriate levels of resource into opportunities and liaise with internal stakeholders such as Customer Success Managers</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conduct structured, deep‑dive discovery sessions to identify/clarify customer objectives, technical challenges, risks, and desired business outcomes.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Uncover explicit and latent requirements using advanced questioning and active listening techniques.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate discovery insights into tailored architectures and solution recommendations aligned to customer needs, timelines, and strategic goals.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Position technical outcomes in terms of operational efficiency, risk reduction, and total cost of ownership benefits.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver high‑impact, outcome‑driven demonstrations that resonate with the customer’s stated priorities.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and lead PoCs with clear success criteria, technical validation milestones, and structured paths to closure.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate complex technical concepts clearly to both technical and non‑technical audiences.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create and deliver engaging presentations that demonstrate Sophos’ value and differentiation.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tailor messaging to senior stakeholders, influencers, and hands‑on practitioners.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent Sophos at events, webinars, and field activities with confidence and clarity.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish rapport quickly with new customers and position Sophos as a long‑term strategic partner.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offer unbiased, advisory‑led recommendations grounded in discovery outcomes and market understanding.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with account executives, product specialists, and product teams to shape competitive strategy.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support demand‑generation campaigns and activities focused on new business acquisition.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain up‑to‑date knowledge of competitor technologies and articulate Sophos’ differentiators with authority.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide insights from customer engagements to influence product direction and go‑to‑market strategy.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engage with customers across the UK and Ireland.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Travel expected to be approximately 25%–50%.</p></li></ul><h2><br />What You'll Bring</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven technical pre‑sales experience in cybersecurity or a closely related field.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to articulate the value of a multi‑product security portfolio across endpoint, MDR/XDR, network, email, identity, and cloud.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional discovery capabilities, including identifying explicit and hidden customer needs.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to run structured discovery conversations that uncover business drivers, pain points, risks, and success criteria.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Capability to convert discovery findings into solution designs and persuasive technical narratives.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong verbal and written communication skills across technical and executive audiences.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confident in building and delivering engaging demonstrations, workshops, and technical evaluations.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Skilled in simplifying complex concepts and presenting them with clarity, impact, and relevance.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to tailor messaging for different stakeholders — from CISOs to analysts and architects.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable building influence, understanding, and trust from scratch within greenfield accounts.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Skilled at guiding organisations with no prior Sophos experience through a structured evaluation process.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep understanding of cybersecurity trends and common customer challenges.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to provide balanced, customer‑centric guidance and establish long‑term technical trust.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Capable of working independently in the field while collaborating effectively across the sales ecosystem.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to manage multiple concurrent workstreams — PoCs, demos, meetings — with strong organisation and prioritisation.</p></li></ul><div style="text-align:left"><img style="max-width:100%" src="data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAlsAAAABCAYAAADpT2vJAAAAAXNSR0IArs4c6QAAAARnQU1BAACxjwv8YQUAAAAJcEhZcwAADsMAAA7DAcdvqGQAAAAZSURBVEhL7cExAQAAAMKg9U9tCj8gAABeagltAAHvBUYeAAAAAElFTkSuQmCC" width="601" height="0" /></div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Relevant Knowledge Areas</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">MDR / XDR</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Network Security</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Endpoint Security / EDR</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cloud (AWS, Azure, GCP)</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Microsoft Security Stack</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What does remote mean at Sophos?<br /></strong>Sophos supports flexible ways of working, with many roles offered remotely and others working in a hybrid model. For remote roles, you may work remotely within the location specified in the job posting. Candidates must reside in and be authorized to work in that location. Our teams collaborate across locations and time zones, using technology to stay connected and deliver results.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Commitment To You</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sophos welcomes applicants with diverse experiences, perspectives, and backgrounds. We believe great ideas come from different ways of thinking, and we are committed to building a workplace where people can contribute, grow, and succeed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We evaluate all candidates based on job-related skills, qualifications, and experience, and are committed to providing equal employment opportunities consistent with applicable laws and regulations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you require a reasonable accommodation during any stage of the recruitment process, please let your recruiter know. Any information shared will be used only to evaluate and provide the requested accommodation.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/sophos/senior-sales-engineer-focus-enterprise-united-kingdom-139528","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom","created_at":1794454816},{"slug":"product-designer-london-118406","company_name":"Letly","title":"Product Designer","description":"<h1><strong>About Aravis</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are building a vertically integrated, AI-native property operations and financial services business serving landlords and tenants. Letly runs rental homes end to end; Aravis is building the accounts, payments and finance around those relationships.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our ambition is to make managing money and financing a home radically easier and cheaper. We’re a small, AI-native team in London, building for global scale.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>The role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll own the user experience of Aravis, turning complex financial tasks into clear, usable journeys. Working directly with the founders, product owners and engineers, you’ll take problems from research through to tested, shipped experiences.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for exceptional UX judgement: understanding how people navigate, interpret information, make decisions and recover when something goes wrong.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>What you’ll own</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer understanding:</strong> speak to landlords and tenants, observe how they complete tasks and identify where they struggle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Journeys and information architecture:</strong> organise the product and design coherent flows across onboarding, accounts, payments, cards and lending.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Interaction design:</strong> make balances, fees, choices and transaction states understandable. Design for errors, delays and recovery as carefully as successes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Prototyping and validation:</strong> explore alternatives, build interactive prototypes and run usability tests. Refine designs through observed behaviour and evidence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shipped quality:</strong> work through details with engineers, review implementation and use completion rates, errors and customer feedback to improve the live product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Consistent patterns:</strong> develop reusable components and interactions that make the product easier to learn and use as it grows.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An outstanding UX portfolio of shipped products, with case studies showing the problem, your decisions, the testing and what improved.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong information architecture and interaction design, particularly across complex workflows and multiple product states.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience conducting customer research and usability testing yourself, and translating findings into better designs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to simplify an experience while preserving the information customers need to make sound decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in Figma, interactive prototyping and design systems, with effective use of AI to explore and test ideas.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong attention to accessibility, product language and visual clarity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear communication and sound judgement when working through commercial, technical and risk constraints with others.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing financial products or similarly complex customer journeys is useful.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>How we work</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Agency:</strong> we move fast, own outcomes, and take responsibility for our work end to end.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Craft:</strong> we go deep on problems and build with care, down to the smallest detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Intensity:</strong> we outwork our competition and continually raise our team’s talent density.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ambition:</strong> we pursue big goals and push ourselves to solve the hardest problems.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work together in our London office and expect a high baseline commitment of time, energy and focus. Sustained intensity is an essential part of how we will win.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>Benefits</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private health insurance, paid gym membership, three meals a day in the office, and Ubers home on late nights.</p><hr><p>Compensation: £110K – £140K</p><ul><li> • £110K – £140K</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/letly/product-designer-london-118406","tags":["Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794454815},{"slug":"principal-ceo-office-london-438305","company_name":"Checkout.com","title":"Principal, CEO Office","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Company Description</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We’re</em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://checkout.com"><em> </em></a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><em>Checkout.com</em></a><em>. You might not know our name, but companies like eBay, Spotify, Klarna, Uber, and Sony do, because we’re behind many of the digital experiences you use every day. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><em>We are where the world checks out, enabling over 10 billion transactions yearly for more than one billion global shoppers. </em><br /><br /><em>Whether you want to book a holiday, order food, renew a subscription, or check out online, there’s a good chance our tech powers the payments behind the scenes. Our platform helps the most ambitious businesses deliver effortless digital experiences, at scale. </em><br /><br /><em>If you want to do career-defining work, you’ve come to the right place. We move fast, think globally, and believe great teams are built by hiring exceptional people with conviction, curiosity, and the desire to make an impact. </em><br /><br /><em>With 20 offices across six continents and London as our HQ, we’re shaping the future of fintech – and we’re just getting started.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The CEO Office</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The CEO Office works with senior leaders across <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a> on high-priority strategic and operational problems. The team turns important questions into clear decisions, coordinated execution and measurable business outcomes.</p><h2>The role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a manager-level individual-contributor role for a hands-on operator. You will own defined, high-priority, cross-functional initiatives end to end—from framing problems and aligning stakeholders to implementing solutions and delivering measurable outcomes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working closely with the Head of the CEO Office, you will combine structured problem-solving with hands-on execution. You will translate priorities into coordinated action, strengthen how teams operate and drive initiatives through to impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is neither a traditional PMO nor a presentation-led strategy role, and it is not an executive-level position. Success requires sound judgement, analytical rigour, clear communication, operational follow-through and the ability to influence effectively without formal authority.</p><h2>How You'll Make an Impact (Role overview)</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the CEO and Head of the CEO Office on critical cross-functional initiatives by helping coordinate day-to-day delivery, stakeholder collaboration and progress towards measurable outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help investigate complex, ambiguous problems by clarifying the problem, developing practical solutions and supporting the implementation of durable processes or systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support departments in scaling by contributing to organisation design, objectives and KPI setting, and the development of robust operating processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assist leadership in navigating ambiguity by surfacing insights, decisions and risks, coordinating follow-through and supporting alignment across teams, particularly where there is no natural owner.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Projects may include organisational model design, international expansion strategy, scaling new business lines, strategic planning and goal setting, go-to-market execution, regulatory, data and financial infrastructure initiatives, and supporting board and shareholder reporting.</p></li></ul><h2>What We're Looking For (Background and core competencies)</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Relevant background and impact:</strong> Experience in a fast-paced, high-performance environment.Relevant backgrounds include consulting, high-growth technology, investing, investment banking, strategic finance or entrepreneurial operations. Payments or fintech exposure and international experience are advantages.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Problem-solving and analytical rigour:</strong> Use first-principles thinking, data and judgement to structure ambiguous problems, identify key measures and move between strategic questions and operational detail. Advanced SQL or hands-on data analysis is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Building and execution:</strong> Turn analysis into practical plans, KPIs, processes, tools or systems that create durable value. Experience building low-code/no-code or AI automations that others continue to use is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership and impact:</strong> Personally own cross-functional work and deliver measurable outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Influence and collaboration:</strong> Build trust, navigate trade-offs and make progress across functions without formal authority, with a low-ego and collaborative approach.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning agility and entrepreneurial mindset:</strong> Learn quickly, respond well to feedback, adapt to changing priorities and show evidence of creating, launching or materially improving something from scratch. Founding or entrepreneurial experience is valued but not required.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring all of you to work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We create the conditions for high performers to thrive, through real ownership, fewer blockers, and work that makes a difference from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here, you’ll move fast, take on meaningful challenges, and be recognized for the impact you deliver. It’s a place where ambition gets met with opportunity, and where your growth is in your hands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work as one team, and we back each other to succeed. So whatever your background or identity, if you’re ready to grow and make a difference, you’ll be right at home here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s important we set you up for success and make our process as accessible as possible. So let us know in your application, or tell your recruiter directly, if you need anything to make your experience or working environment more comfortable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Life at </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><strong>Checkout.com</strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We understand that work is just one part of your life. Our hybrid working model offers flexibility, with three days per week in the office to support collaboration and connection.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious about what it’s like to be part of our team? Visit our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.checkout.com/careers"> <u>Careers Page</u></a> to learn more about our culture, open roles, and what drives us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For a closer look at daily life at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>, follow us on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/checkout/life/"><u>LinkedIn</u></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.instagram.com/checkout_com/"><u>Instagram</u></a></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/checkoutcom/principal-ceo-office-london-438305","tags":["All Departments"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794454815},{"slug":"senior-cloud-engineer-i-london-78871","company_name":"Checkout.com","title":"Senior Cloud Engineer I","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Company Description</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We’re</em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://checkout.com"><em> </em></a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><em>Checkout.com</em></a><em>. You might not know our name, but companies like eBay, Spotify, Klarna, Uber, and Sony do, because we’re behind many of the digital experiences you use every day. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><em>We are where the world checks out, enabling over 10 billion transactions yearly for more than one billion global shoppers. </em><br /><br /><em>Whether you want to book a holiday, order food, renew a subscription, or check out online, there’s a good chance our tech powers the payments behind the scenes. Our platform helps the most ambitious businesses deliver effortless digital experiences, at scale. </em><br /><br /><em>If you want to do career-defining work, you’ve come to the right place. We move fast, think globally, and believe great teams are built by hiring exceptional people with conviction, curiosity, and the desire to make an impact. </em><br /><br /><em>With 20 offices across six continents and London as our HQ, we’re shaping the future of fintech – and we’re just getting started.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every payment we process runs on infrastructure we built. At <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>, the Cloud Platform team owns the cloud foundations that global payments depend on: a large multi-account AWS estate, a growing Azure platform, and the networking and connectivity that reaches card schemes and banks worldwide. We are genuinely multi-cloud, and we are looking for a Senior Cloud Engineer who is too - a strong generalist who treats infrastructure as a software problem and can deliver from week one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on senior role in an established, fast-moving team. Everything we run is defined in code, deployed through pipelines, and reviewed like software. You will bring deep cloud expertise across AWS and Azure and pair it with a genuine software engineering mindset: you write Terraform modules others build on, you automate away toil rather than documenting it, and you treat the platform as a product with users, SLOs, and a roadmap.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Senior Cloud Engineer, you are responsible for the technical delivery of your team's services. You will work closely with your Engineering Manager to shape direction, manage dependencies across pillars, and ensure our platform meets the standards a regulated payments business demands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we are looking for:</strong><br /><br />Deep AWS expertise: Advanced, hands-on experience designing and operating production infrastructure in AWS at enterprise scale: multi-account architectures (Control Tower, Organizations, SCPs), IAM, KMS, and the core compute, storage, and security services that a large regulated estate runs on. You should have a proven track record of delivering resilient, multi-region architectures.<br /><br />Azure experience: Real production experience with Azure alongside AWS: landing zones, VNet architectures, Entra ID, and the Azure resource and governance model. You understand where the two clouds differ and can design well for both rather than forcing one cloud's patterns onto the other.<br /><br />Software engineering mindset: You treat infrastructure as software. Expert-level Terraform: reusable modules, secure state management, and disciplined code review. You are comfortable in a Git-based workflow with CI/CD (we use Spacelift), and you reach for Python or similar to automate what others would handle with a runbook. No ClickOps.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong cloud networking: Confident designing and debugging in a complex network estate: VPC and VNet design, hub-and-spoke and Transit Gateway or Cloud WAN architectures, DNS, private connectivity (PrivateLink, Private Link), and enough routing knowledge to own connectivity issues end to end rather than escalate them.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Kubernetes: Solid experience running containerised workloads in production, ideally on EKS/AKS: cluster lifecycle, workload deployment patterns, and the operational realities of keeping Kubernetes healthy at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Security and compliance awareness: Experience operating in regulated environments. You understand why change control, least privilege, and auditability matter, and you design controls in rather than bolting them on. Familiarity with PCI DSS is a strong plus.<br /><br />Engineering excellence: A focus on observability and measurement: you instrument what you build and answer operational questions with data rather than opinion.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leadership and mentorship: A natural ability to guide and mentor peers, translate ambiguous problem definitions into actionable technical plans, and raise the bar through your code and your reviews.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pragmatic problem solver: You understand when to move fast (creating tech debt) and when to move right (paying it off). You are a cornerstone in incident resolution and root-cause analysis.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience: 5+ years in cloud engineering roles with significant AWS depth. We need someone who can hit the ground running: comfortable joining a complex, established estate and delivering meaningful work in their first weeks, not their first quarter. A degree in Computer Science or a related field is useful but not required; we care about what you can build.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>How you’ll make an impact:</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead Design &amp; Delivery: Take ownership of large-scale platform projects end to end, from architecture through Terraform to production, ensuring they are scalable, secure, and cost-optimised.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the paved road: Design the platform primitives that every product team at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a> builds on, so that the secure path is also the easy path.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Architectural Influence:  Work with Engineering Managers and architects to refine requirements and shape the technical direction of the platform, documenting significant decisions as ADRs.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Operational SME: Act as the Subject Matter Expert for numerous team-owned services, providing advanced operational support and ensuring high availability for our global payment systems.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evangelise Best Practices: Produce exemplary code and documentation that inspires others. You will be responsible for spreading best practices and standards across your group.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage Dependencies: Navigate the organisation to manage technical dependencies inside and outside your pillar, optimising for both delivery speed and business outcomes.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Foster Culture: Embody Checkout Operating Principles, using them to shape the group’s culture and acting as an example of efficiency and professional excellence.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI Integration: Proactively explore and implement AI-driven automation to enhance infrastructure efficiency and team productivity.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring all of you to work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We create the conditions for high performers to thrive, through real ownership, fewer blockers, and work that makes a difference from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here, you’ll move fast, take on meaningful challenges, and be recognized for the impact you deliver. It’s a place where ambition gets met with opportunity, and where your growth is in your hands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work as one team, and we back each other to succeed. So whatever your background or identity, if you’re ready to grow and make a difference, you’ll be right at home here.</p