em">The ideal candidate is an independent, high-achieving individual, able to stand out in an ambitious environment and excel through self-motivation and personal drive. If you are eager to join a thriving, fast-paced environment this is the role for you to make a difference.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How you’ll make an impact</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Grow a portfolio of existing enterprise merchants by identifying expansion opportunities, cross/upselling Checkout’s value add services, performance improvements, and other levers to increase our share of wallet.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Crafting and executing on merchant specific account development plans, outlining clear opportunities for growth and paths to success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building high touch, consultative, and nurturing relationships with our merchants through regular and open communications, both face-to-face and virtual.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Delivering expertise, education, and guidance to merchants. Act as their payment consultant as they craft and complete a comprehensive, global payments strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Negotiate win-win pricing structures by growing a thorough overview of a merchant's revenue drivers to deliver the best, sustainable outcomes for both merchant and Checkout.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tracking merchant project deliverables and ensure merchant activities are updated within SalesForce, Clari, and other CRM tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding the intricacies of our products, services and partner networks thoroughly to leverage this against our merchants’ growing needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborating with various teams (e.g. Sales, Legal, Integration, Support) across the company to ensure an outstanding merchant experience and bring the voice of the customer to our internal stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Data-based decision making - not afraid of diving into numbers to ensure merchants have confidence in our ability to provide meaningful and metric-driven insights.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive a culture of cross-team learning through active knowledge sharing whilst contributing to improving ways of working, impacting not just ‘what’ we do but ‘how’ we do it.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Qualifications</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience: 3+ years’ commercial experience in a B2B Account Management or Relationship Management role in the FinTech and/or Payments industry.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercial Acumen: Proven track record of driving and exceeding revenue targets and managing strategic account portfolios. Experience in negotiating and pricing strategy deals specific to the UK market.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Payments Knowledge: Good knowledge of today’s major e-commerce and payments, technologies, players and major future trends.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Customer Obsession: Customer driven and able to establish a robust relationship with assigned customer base.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Multifaceted approach adapting to changing requirements with the ability to balance multiple opportunities concurrently.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring all of you to work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We create the conditions for high performers to thrive, through real ownership, fewer blockers, and work that makes a difference from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here, you’ll move fast, take on meaningful challenges, and be recognized for the impact you deliver. It’s a place where ambition gets met with opportunity, and where your growth is in your hands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work as one team, and we back each other to succeed. So whatever your background or identity, if you’re ready to grow and make a difference, you’ll be right at home here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s important we set you up for success and make our process as accessible as possible. So let us know in your application, or tell your recruiter directly, if you need anything to make your experience or working environment more comfortable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Life at </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><strong>Checkout.com</strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We understand that work is just one part of your life. Our hybrid working model offers flexibility, with three days per week in the office to support collaboration and connection.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious about what it’s like to be part of our team? Visit our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.checkout.com/careers"> <u>Careers Page</u></a> to learn more about our culture, open roles, and what drives us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For a closer look at daily life at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>, follow us on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/checkout/life/"><u>LinkedIn</u></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.instagram.com/checkout_com/"><u>Instagram</u></a></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/checkoutcom/senior-specialist-account-management-london-163151","tags":["All Departments"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794454815},{"slug":"product-marketing-lead-london-365326","company_name":"Cuspai","title":"Product Marketing Lead","description":"<h2>About CuspAI </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">CuspAI is the frontier AI company on a mission to solve the breakthrough materials needed to power human progress. While nature took billions of years to perfect molecules, we are harnessing AI to unlock trillion-dollar materials breakthroughs in months, not millennia. Our founding team is the most cited in the world, comprised of world-class researchers in AI, chemistry and engineering.<br /><br />We are working on some of the hardest and most important challenges including energy, clean water, the future of compute, and carbon capture, and this is just the start of what our 'search engine' for next-generation materials will unlock.<br /><br />We invite you to be part of a diverse, innovative team at the intersection of AI and materials science, working to create impactful partnerships that drive innovation, scalability, and industry collaboration. This work matters. Your work matters.<br /><br /><strong>We’re on the cusp of the on-demand materials era. Join us.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Due to rapid growth, we are seeking an experienced <strong>Product Marketing Lead </strong>to own how the world understands our products and ecosystem. They will work closely with the product teams to frame product positioning, commercial narratives, and GTM strategies across our agentic platform, AI Materials Foundry and new products as they emerge.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Your Impact</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role you will be building the product marketing function that transforms CuspAI's deep scientific breakthroughs into clear, credible narratives, accelerating our GTM engine and scaling the global impact of our AI Materials Foundry.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Over time, you will scale the function by hiring, coaching, and leading a high-performing product marketing team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You Will Do</strong><br /></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Platform Launch &amp; Go-to-Market</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the end-to-end launch of science products, from early-access and design-partner programmes through announcement and general availability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan and execute GTM for subsequent releases, new modules, scientific milestones, and strategic ecosystem announcements, building a repeatable launch process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with Product, Commercial and Finance on pricing and packaging.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the product marketing for self-serve adoption, including website product pages, onboarding content and in-product messaging that turn early users into paying customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Comms/PR on press and analyst narratives, Partnerships on co-marketing campaigns, and Creative teams on high-impact visual assets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Co-own narrative alignment and onboarding sessions for new Foundry participants.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product Positioning &amp; Messaging Architecture</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the messaging and naming architecture for new products, the AI Materials Foundry, and emerging product capabilities, working with leadership and Brand as the platform expands through regular releases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build segment- and persona-level messaging tailored to the experimental scientists who use the platform day to day, the technical buyers who sign off on it (e.g. CTOs and Heads of R&amp;D), and Foundry partners (e.g. industrial customers, compute partners, and research labs).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with AI Researchers, Product, and Engineering teams to ensure all performance claims are scientifically defensible and reflect current platform capabilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own competitive positioning against general-purpose AI science assistants and specialist materials-discovery platforms, and keep competitive intelligence current for Commercial, Product and the Founders.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Foundry &amp; Partner Ecosystem Marketing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and articulate the Foundry membership proposition, framing how network effects compound scientific discovery over time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive co-marketing programs with founding and future partners (e.g. joint case studies, event presence, and co-authored thought leadership).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop recurring quantitative proof points that demonstrate real-world validation outcomes and accelerated R&amp;D timelines.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sales Enablement &amp; Customer Intelligence</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equip Commercial and Partnerships teams with pitch decks, one-pagers, and demo scripts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build customer case studies and reference stories in multiple formats.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Must Have Skills &amp; Qualifications</strong><br /></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">8+ years of experience in product marketing within deep tech, scientific software, enterprise AI/ML platforms, semiconductors, or advanced industrial sectors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record of building product positioning, messaging architectures, and GTM frameworks from scratch in high-growth environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated ability to translate highly complex, deep-tech subject matter into clear, rigorous, and compelling commercial narratives without losing scientific accuracy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience managing partner, ecosystem, or multi-sided platform marketing programs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong collaborative skills with experience working cross-functionally alongside scientific researchers, product managers, commercial leaders, and design teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High autonomy and leadership aptitude, with a strong desire to transition from an individual contributor to building and managing a team as the company scales.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Bonus Points (But Not Critical):</strong><br /></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Academic background (BSc, MSc, or PhD) in Chemistry, Materials Science, Physics, Chemical Engineering, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct experience marketing to buyers within semiconductors, chemicals, clean energy, or advanced manufacturing sectors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prior experience navigating scale-up dynamics in a fast-growing, post-Series B technology company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with agentic AI workflows, atomistic simulation tools, or scientific machine learning frameworks.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Additional Considerations</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is ideally based in our <strong>London office</strong> (we would also consider Cambridge, Amsterdam or Berlin), with the expectation of being <strong>in the office three days per week</strong>. Additionally, there may be regular travel required to othe