<li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Processing sales quotes and deadlines in an accurate manner</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working with the marketing and sales team on developing new strategies to grow our sales pipeline based on conversations and input you will be having in the market</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Driving performance to consistently meet monthly, quarterly and annual goals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create new business through network events </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll be bringing:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Relevant sales experience in a Field and outbound environment, preferably in a solution-sales / technology-related</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong experience in hospitality </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of sales development best practices</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to manage time effectively and efficiently</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent customer service and telephone skills, including strong listening, verbal and written communication</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated ability to meet and/or exceed sales targets</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience using Salesforce or comparable CRM experience to manage and organise pipeline</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in English, any other language is a nice to have</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An entrepreneurial and agile mindset, a bias toward action and an ability to pivot when needed to meet business needs and objectives</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>To all recruitment agencies: Lightspeed does not accept unsolicited agency resumes. If we have not directly engaged your company in writing to supply candidates for a specific vacancy, Lightspeed will not be responsible for any fees related to unsolicited resumes.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Lightspeed is a proud equal opportunity employer and we are committed to creating an inclusive and barrier-free workplace. Lightspeed welcomes and encourages applications from people with disabilities. Accommodations are available on request for candidates taking part in all aspects of the selection process.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Where to from here?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Obviously, this has to be mutually beneficial: we want you to step into a role you love, and we want to offer you a place you’re proud to come to every day. For a glimpse into our world check out our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.lightspeedhq.com/careers/">career page here</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed is building communities through commerce, and we need people from all backgrounds and lived experiences to do that. We were founded in 2005, in Montreal’s gay village and our original members were all part of the LGBTQ+ community. The ethos of our business has been about inclusion from the very beginning, and we strive to provide a workplace where everyone belongs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who we are:</strong> </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Powering the businesses that are the backbone of the global economy, Lightspeed's one-stop commerce platform helps merchants innovate to simplify, scale, and provide exceptional customer experiences. Our cloud commerce solution transforms and unifies online and physical operations, multichannel sales, expansion to new locations, global payments, financial solutions, and connection to supplier networks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in Montréal, Canada in 2005, Lightspeed is dual-listed on the New York Stock Exchange (NYSE: LSPD) and Toronto Stock Exchange (TSX: LSPD). With teams across North America, Europe, and Asia Pacific, the company serves retail, hospitality, and golf businesses in over 100 countries.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed handles your information in accordance with our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="c-link" href="https://www.lightspeedhq.com/legal/applicant-privacy-statement/">Applicant Privacy Statement</a>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/lightspeedhq/field-account-executive-glasgow-221822","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Glasgow","created_at":1794444014},{"slug":"head-of-data-kensington-office-london-192477","company_name":"Mulberry","title":"Head of Data","description":"<div><span style="font-size: 16px">Born in 1971, the roots of Mulberry are in Somerset, England. For more than fifty years, Mulberry has been a British lifestyle brand, internationally acclaimed for quality and design capturing the Mulberry Spirit.</span></div><div><br></div><div><span style="font-size: 16px">Sustainability has been part of the Mulberry ethos since the brand's inception, in recognition of our purpose-driven approach, in 2024 we proudly achieved B Corp Certification.&nbsp;</span></div><div><br></div><div><span style="font-size: 16px">Today, we are a global brand, but our values remain the same; we are committed to improving our impact on people and the planet.&nbsp;To do this our people are honest, dynamic, and community spirited.</span></div><div><br></div><div><span style="font-size: 16px">If these are values you share, we would love you to join our team.</span></div><div><br></div><div>
<div>
<p>Mulberry is looking for an experienced Head of Data to establish and lead our enterprise data capability.</p>
<p>This is a pivotal new role with the opportunity to shape how data is architected, governed, managed and used across Mulberry. You will define our data operating model, establish clear ownership and governance, build a cross-functional data community and create the foundations for trusted, accessible and valuable data across the business.</p>
<p>Working closely with senior business leaders and Technology, you will act as the single point of accountability for Data Enablement across Mulberry, ensuring our approach is driven by business priorities and delivers measurable value.</p>
<p>Alongside establishing the organisational capability, you will help shape Mulberry’s future technology data capability. This could involve evolving our existing Google Cloud Platform / BigQuery environment or moving towards an alternative solution. The role will ensure that our business needs, operating model and long-term ambitions inform those choices.</p>
<h2>What you’ll be responsible for</h2>
<ul>
<li>Define and implement Mulberry’s enterprise Data strategy and operating model, including ownership, governance, stewardship and decision rights.</li>
<li>Establish a pragmatic Data Governance framework, covering definitions, quality, lineage, metadata, standards and accountability.</li>
<li>Create and lead a cross-functional Data Community, establishing Data Owners and Data Stewards across key business areas and equipping them with the guidance, training and practical tools needed to fulfil their responsibilities.</li>
<li>Act as the enterprise point of accountability for Data Enablement, bringing together business and Technology priorities.</li>
<li>Lead the business direction of our Data Foundations programme and help transition it into a sustainable, long-term capability.</li>
<li>Establish common definitions, authoritative data sources and trusted enterprise measures, reducing multiple versions of the truth and manual reconciliation.</li>
<li>Work with Technology to define the business requirements and guiding principles for our future data architecture and platform.</li>
<li>Develop a prioritised Data roadmap focused on delivering tangible commercial and operational value.</li>
<li>Build data literacy and enable greater, appropriately governed self-service across the organisation.</li>
<li>Create the foundations required for future analytics, automation and AI opportunities.</li>
<li>Work with relevant Legal and Technology stakeholders to embed appropriate data classification, access, retention and lifecycle controls, with clear ownership of data risks and remediation.</li>
</ul>
<h2>About you</h2>
<p>You’ll combine strong Data expertise with commercial judgement and the ability to lead enterprise-wide change.</p>
<p>We’re looking for someone who has:</p>
<ul>
<li>Significant experience in Data leadership, Data Governance, Data Management or enterprise Data transformation.</li>
<li>Experience building or materially evolving a Data operating model, rather than simply managing an established function.</li>
<li>Strong knowledge of Data Governance, ownership, stewardship, quality, lineage and metadata.</li>
<li>Experience establishing accountability across multiple business functions and building the internal and external capabilities needed to deliver data outcomes.</li>
<li>A strong commercial mindset, with the ability to translate business challenges into clear Data priorities and outcomes.</li>
<li>The confidence to influence senior leaders and constructively challenge both business and technical stakeholders.</li>
<li>Sufficient understanding of modern cloud Data platforms to help shape technology decisions without needing to be the technical architect.</li>
<li>Experience developing Data strategies and investment roadmaps.</li>
<li>Clear, engaging communication skills and the ability to make Data understandable to non-technical audiences.</li>
<li>Knowledge of GCP, BigQuery or comparable cloud data platforms.</li>
</ul>
<p>Experience within retail, luxury, consumer goods or manufacturing would be advantageous.</p>
<h2>What success looks like</h2>
<p>Within your first year, you will have established:</p>
<ul>
<li>A clear and functioning enterprise Data operating model.</li>
<li>Active Data Owners and Data Stewards across priority areas.</li>
<li>A strong cross-functional Data Community.</li>
<li>Common definitions and governance for critical enterprise data and KPIs.</li>
<li>Improved visibility of Data quality, lineage, ownership and risk.</li>
<li>A prioritised Data roadmap linked to measurable business outcomes.</li>
<li>A clear future technology Data capability and supporting organisational model.</li>
<li>Greater trust in and use of Data for decision-making across Mulberry.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Why this role matters</h2>
<p>This is not a traditional reporting, BI or technical Data role. It is an opportunity to build an enterprise capability from the ground up.</p>
<p>Data is increasingly critical to how Mulberry makes commercial and operational decisions, and to how we develop our future technology and AI capabilities. The Head of Data will play a central role in creating the ownership, governance, capability and culture needed to unlock that opportunity.</p>
