About us
<p>Troostwijk & the TBAuctions group are part of one of Europe’s leading networks for digital B2B auctions. We market machines, vehicles, equipment and other commercial assets, bringing sellers and buyers together through digital processes and personal support.</p>
What your day-to-day work will involve
<p>As an Account Manager, you will develop the French seller market and act as the main point of contact for new and existing sellers. You will build a profitable portfolio, develop long-term relationships based on trust and guide opportunities from the first conversation through to active auction business.</p>
<p>The role combines remote work with regular travel and gives you direct influence on the development of our French market.</p>
<p>You will receive professional support from our teams and work with modern tools that help you structure your pipeline, follow-ups and seller relationships.</p>
<h2>What this means in practice</h2>
<ul>
<li>Identify, approach and acquire new sellers in the French market.</li>
<li>Develop a profitable seller portfolio and build long-term relationships based on trust.</li>
<li>Research companies and market opportunities and turn them into relevant conversations.</li>
<li>Present our activities and value proposition clearly to business owners and potential sellers.</li>
<li>Prepare meetings, understand seller needs and agree on clear next steps.</li>
<li>Own negotiations and follow opportunities through to conversion.</li>
<li>Keep pipeline, follow-ups and seller information structured with modern tools.</li>
<li>Represent our company image and values in the market and coordinate closely with internal teams.</li>
</ul>
What matters in this role
<p>We are looking for someone who enjoys building a market rather than only maintaining an existing portfolio. You should be comfortable creating your own pipeline, speaking confidently with business owners, handling rejection and staying focused until opportunities move forward.</p>
<h2>What you should bring</h2>
<ul>
<li>Proven experience in sales, business development or new-business acquisition.</li>
<li>Experience in a technical, industrial or B2B environment with measurable commercial results.</li>
<li>Strong communication, negotiation, closing and relationship-building skills.</li>
<li>Autonomy, commercial drive, persistence and a results-oriented approach.</li>
<li>Willingness to travel regularly and a valid Category B driving licence.</li>
<li>French as a native language and the ability to work in English.</li>
</ul>
<p>A perfect CV is less important than your ability to create relationships, develop a territory and turn commercial opportunities into long-term seller business.</p>
<h2>What we offer</h2>
<h2>Autonomy with professional support</h2>
<p>You will own your territory and your seller relationships while working closely with internal teams that support you with expertise, coordination and operational follow-through. You will not be left alone with complex opportunities or process questions.</p>
<h2>Build something with visible impact</h2>
<p>The role gives you the opportunity to help establish the French market, shape long-term seller relationships and contribute directly to recurring auction activity. Your work combines commercial ownership with professional development.</p>
<h2>Performance that pays off</h2>
<p>You can expect an attractive compensation package with a competitive fixed salary and a bonus model that recognises your individual performance.</p>
<h2>Your benefits</h2>
<p>Company car, computer, phone and meal tickets support you in your day-to-day work.</p>
<p><em><strong>Do you have a track record in B2B sales and want to help build the French seller market? We look forward to hearing from you.</strong></em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/surplex-gmbh/accountmanager-in-auction-business-hauts-de-france-gn-lille-242834","tags":["Remote","Business Development"],"job_types":["Permanent employment","professional / experienced"],"location":"Lille","created_at":1794412866},{"slug":"senior-account-executive-hotels-france-netherlands-12m-ftc-paris-297976","company_name":"airbnb","title":"Senior Account Executive, Hotels - France & Netherlands (12M FTC)","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Airbnb Hotels team is a fun, fast-growing group leading Airbnb’s expansion into the hotel sector. Operating with an entrepreneurial spirit, this team combines the simplicity, product excellence, and guest-centered ethos that define Airbnb. This team’s mission is to deliver the smoothest, most intuitive hotel booking experience for guests, while helping independent, boutique hotels easily drive incremental bookings so they can focus on delivering the best hospitality. The ultimate aim is to help more people discover high-quality hotels, creating value for guests and our hotel partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Account Executive, you will be responsible for converting leads into net‑new supply to support new-market launches and at pace to hit quarterly goals. Working the full sales funnel, you will proactively turn cold leads into warm sales opportunities helping to build the Hotels category’s market presence in the process through collaboration with other teams. This includes partnering, strategizing, and running daily operations directly with independent, boutique hotels , and ensuring that Airbnb sources&amp;nbsp; the best hotel inventory available to our guests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in Paris (hybrid, 2 days a week in the office).&amp;nbsp; It will start off as a 12-month FTC with the potential for conversion depending on individual performance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet and exceed KPIs by owning the performance and success of assigned region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prospect new potential hotels through external research, networking, and use of Airbnb tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Securing new hotels involves targeted sales strategies and negotiating and closing the deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develops acquisition strategies and scalable, localised supply strategies for established and emerging markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertly position and communicate Airbnb’s value proposition to new partners via phone, email, and in-person&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add net new hotels by qualifying and moving leads through the funnel as quickly as possible, achieving defined quarterly goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find supply in and launch new markets: Own market launches including supporting lead generation and coordinating cross functionally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support hotel onboarding as needed from won sales opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively promote and build strong relationships with hotels by demonstrating comprehensive knowledge of our platforms and confidently pitching their value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of professional experience, preferably in a fast growing startup tech or hospitality company working in sales and/or account management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous hospitality experience is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in both English and French.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CRM required; Proficiency in Salesforce, Gong and other scalable AI Sales prospecting tools is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to get things done with constantly changing priorities, projects and deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, organizational, and analytical skills, detail-oriented but moves fast&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to establish strong relationships with and influence partners&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capacity to balance day-to-day responsibilities with longer-term strategic execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a quick learner and you’re fearless about doing whatever it takes to get the job done, even if it means making mistakes along the way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to travel up to 25-30% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for Airbnb and travel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We’ll Take Care of You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our job titles may span more than one career level. The actual base pay is dependent upon many factors, such as: training, transferable skills, work experience, business needs and market demands. The base pay range is subject to change and may be modified in the future. This role may also be eligible for variable incentive pay, benefits, and Employee Travel Credits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The On-Target Earnings (“OTE”) range for this role is €98,000 to €115,000 gross per year, which includes a split of 80% (base pay) / 20% (variable incentive).&amp;nbsp;Of this OTE amount, the annual gross base salary range is €78,400 to €92,000.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The OTE reflected on this job posting is the target cash compensation a candidate could earn in a year if they achieve 100% of their performance or sales goals. The variable incentive is not guaranteed and is governed by the terms of Airbnb’s Hotels Variable Compensation Plan (the “Plan”). The actual payouts depend on performance against targets set under the “Plan” and may be higher or lower than the range listed on this job posting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment To Inclusion &amp;amp; Belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reasonable Accommodations:&lt;/strong&gt; We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process for applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or an accommodation, please let your recruiter know once you are contacted about a role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Note on Recruiting Scams:&lt;/strong&gt; Scammers sometimes pose as Airbnb recruiters to get money or personal information from candidates. A few things that will always be true for Airbnb’s hiring process: our open roles are posted on Airbnb’s Career’s Page at careers.airbnb.com, and our recruiters correspond only from @&lt;a href=&quot;http://airbnb.com&quot;&gt;airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; or @&lt;a href=&quot;http://ext.airbnb.com&quot;&gt;ext.airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; email addresses. Our recruiters will never ask for your Social Security number, bank account details, passport, or payment app information while you are interviewing.&amp;nbsp; We’ll also never ask you to pay a fee, send money, deposit or cash a check, or purchase work-related equipment (such as a company laptop) during the interview process. We encourage candidates to remain vigilant of these recruiting scams and not share sensitive information if you do not believe an individual is actually affiliated with Airbnb.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/airbnb/senior-account-executive-hotels-france-netherlands-12m-ftc-paris-297976","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":[],"location":"Paris","created_at":1794412533},{"slug":"marketing-crm-intern-experiences-paris-396246","company_name":"airbnb","title":"Marketing & CRM Intern, Experiences","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The community you will join:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb is looking for a Marketing &amp;amp; CRM intern to join the Experiences team in Paris for a 6-month internship.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work directly with the person in charge of Demand for Paris Experiences, alongside Marketing, Growth and Product Management partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experiences let guests step into the real life of a destination: cook with a local chef, explore a hidden neighborhood with a historian, discover Paris through the eyes of the people who live there. Paris is one of our most iconic and competitive markets, and our job on the Demand side is to make sure the right guests find the right Experience at the right moment, whether they are visiting Paris or live nearby.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a curious, organized and data-friendly student who loves the craft of CRM and Operational Marketing: a sharp brief, a well-built email, a smart audience, and an analysis that tells us what to do next. You are comfortable juggling several campaigns at once, working with different teams, and turning numbers into clear recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The difference you will make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will support the Paris Experiences Demand lead on the day-to-day CRM and marketing activity that drives bookings. You will see a campaign from the first brief to the final analysis, and you will own your own projects along the way. During your internship, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Run email campaigns end to end&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write briefs for email campaigns (audience, objective, key messages, timing) and coordinate with copy, design and CRM partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute campaigns through our internal tools and planning process, including setup, QA and send follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze results after each send (opens, clicks, bookings, incrementality) and share clear learnings and next steps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Support listing promotion and audience targeting&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze cohorts of guests (new vs. returning, local vs. traveler, International vs Domestic) to understand behavior over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build simple, readable dashboards and recurring reports to select and prioritize listings based on quality, availability, performance and fit with the campaign&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Market and Supply teams to make sure what we promote is bookable and best-in-class&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn insights into concrete recommendations for audiences, timing and messaging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Follow local activations&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide operational support and follow-up on field campaigns such as flyering, partnerships, events or more: briefing, logistics, timing, partners and results tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help measure what works locally and recommend future iterations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The intern experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an intern, you will be part of a team where you contribute to real projects with real business impact. Your manager, your team and our wider employee community will strive to be superhosts to you during your internship. We provide the support, mentorship and hands-on experience you need to learn quickly and make an impact.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll get a front-row seat on how a global marketplace builds demand for a destination, with real ownership from day one: your campaigns go live and your analyses shape decisions. You’ll do it alongside a team that cares about craft, curiosity and human connection. You can expect to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Marketing, Market Management and Acquisition partners to deliver projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present your analyses and recommendations to stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Seek and give feedback throughout the internship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take part in the Experiences and broader Airbnb community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Current student or recent graduate&lt;/strong&gt; (degree completed within the last 12 months) from a leading business school, engineering school or equivalent program in France, looking for a 6-month internship starting in January 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fluent in French and English&lt;/strong&gt;, with excellent written communication: you can write a clear brief and a clear recap. You also have an eye for great copy and for what makes a message feel human&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A strong interest in marketing, CRM or growth&lt;/strong&gt;, and in travel, hospitality or community-driven products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Curious about data and performance metrics&lt;/strong&gt;, with an interest in using insights and quantitative analysis to evaluate campaigns, track performance, and inform decision-making. Experience with Claude or other AI tools to work faster and smarter is a must-have.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Highly organized and detail-oriented&lt;/strong&gt;, able to manage several campaigns and deadlines in parallel, and to follow up until everything is done&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A collaborative mindset &lt;/strong&gt;and the confidence to work with people across teams, from Marketing to Product to Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have work authorization for France. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Due to the nature of this position, the successful applicant will need to be based in Paris, France to be able to conduct their work. Interns can expect to spend half of their time at the office and half working remotely with exact dates as agreed upon by the hiring manager. Additional in-person attendance for team meetings or offsites may be required as needed. Please note we are unable to provide relocation or visa sponsorship for this position.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our commitment to inclusion &amp;amp; belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;How We&#39;ll Take Care of You:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base pay range shown below is annualized, is subject to change and may be modified in the future.&amp;nbsp; This role may also be eligible for benefits and Employee Travel Credits.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;France Annual Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€25.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€25.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reasonable Accommodations:&lt;/strong&gt; We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process for applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or an accommodation, please let your recruiter know once you are contacted about a role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Note on Recruiting Scams:&lt;/strong&gt; Scammers sometimes pose as Airbnb recruiters to get money or personal information from candidates. A few things that will always be true for Airbnb’s hiring process: our open roles are posted on Airbnb’s Career’s Page at careers.airbnb.com, and our recruiters correspond only from @&lt;a href=&quot;http://airbnb.com&quot;&gt;airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; or @&lt;a href=&quot;http://ext.airbnb.com&quot;&gt;ext.airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; email addresses. Our recruiters will never ask for your Social Security number, bank account details, passport, or payment app information while you are interviewing.&amp;nbsp; We’ll also never ask you to pay a fee, send money, deposit or cash a check, or purchase work-related equipment (such as a company laptop) during the interview process. We encourage candidates to remain vigilant of these recruiting scams and not share sensitive information if you do not believe an individual is actually affiliated with Airbnb.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/airbnb/marketing-crm-intern-experiences-paris-396246","tags":["Intern"],"job_types":[],"location":"Paris","created_at":1794412533},{"slug":"senior-talent-partner-tech-paris-5757","company_name":"Dust","title":"Senior Talent Partner, Tech","description":"<h1><strong>About Dust</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work is being rewritten, and the people holding the pen are the ones who actually run it.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With enterprise-grade governance, flexible model choice, and a collaborative interface for humans and agents to work together, Dust empowers AI Operators at the world’s fastest-moving companies to rewire how work gets done.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With 70%+ weekly active users, people stick with Dust as much as they do with Slack and Notion. We don't get piloted and shelved. We land once, and spread. <strong>We're at an exciting stage of our journey, and growing fast.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're serving <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://dust.tt/customers">great customers</a> like Datadog, 1Password, Cursor, Clay, Vanta and Persona, and aim to x5 our growth by the end of 2026.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dust is backed by <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://techcrunch.com/2024/06/27/dust-grabs-another-16-million-for-its-enterprise-ai-assistants-connected-to-internal-data/">Sequoia</a> with a determined team of optimists (coming from Stripe, OpenAI, and Stanford) who like to focus on users, ship fast, and don't take themselves too seriously while doing so. The Generalist <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/posts/dust-tt_were-honored-to-be-recognized-on-the-generalists-activity-7359284343929741313-Rq04">named us among the Future 50</a>.</p><h1><strong>Why this role exists</strong></h1><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are about to hire the people who will define the next phase of this company. Not backfill a plan someone else wrote — define it. The quality of who joins Dust over the next eighteen months is the single highest-leverage variable in whether we build the category or watch someone else do it.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">That work needs a recruiter who treats hiring as a craft rather than a queue. Someone who can hold a real point of view on what "great" looks like for a role, defend it with a hiring manager who disagrees, and then go find that person themselves — from a cold start, without a lead gen team, a sourcing pod, or a playbook waiting for them.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll be an early member of a small Talent team. That means you own roles end to end, and you also help build the thing itself: the assessment design, the interview loops, the calibration, the data we use to know whether any of it is working.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for someone who cares about the candidate experience for all parties internal and external. And prioritizes protecting Dust's culture by being thoughtful, thorough and leading by example in being a true team player.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>What you'll own</strong></h1><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Full-cycle hiring, end to end.</strong> You run your own searches from role kickoff to close. Sourcing, outreach, screening, interviewing, offer strategy, negotiation. You are the owner of the outcome, not a coordinator of other people's opinions.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Assessment design, not just assessment delivery.</strong> For every role you open, you help define what evidence would actually predict success — then you build the loop that surfaces it. You'll push back on interview stages that exist out of habit and replace them with ones that test something real.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hiring manager partnership with a spine.</strong> You'll spend as much time calibrating hiring managers as you do talking to candidates. When a manager says "not quite the right feel," you'll ask what they mean until there's a defensible answer, and you'll say so when there isn't one.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Market intelligence.</strong> You'll know your talent market better than anyone else in the building — who's good, where they are, what moves them, what compensation actually looks like right now — and you'll bring that back into how we scope roles and design offers.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The candidate experience.</strong> Our hiring process is the first honest sample of what working here feels like. You'll make it expedient, direct, well-communicated, and worth a candidate's time whether or not they get an offer.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Building the function.</strong> Process, tooling, structured scorecards, funnel data, quality-of-hire signal. You'll leave the system better than you found it, and you'll be trusted to change it without asking permission first.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>Two tracks — tell us which one is yours</strong></h1><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're hiring for depth in one of two areas. You should have a genuine centre of gravity in one; interest in the other is a bonus, not a requirement.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>GTM.</strong> Account Executives, Sales Engineers, Customer Success, Marketing, and the leaders above them, across Europe and the US. You know how to assess commercial talent on evidence rather than swagger, and you can tell the difference between a rep who carried a territory and a rep who inherited one.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical.</strong> Software engineers, infrastructure, product, and design, in a market where the best people are not looking and the second-best are drowning in outreach. You can hold a credible conversation about what someone actually built, and you know why that matters more than where they built it.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>How we think about hiring</strong></h1><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're telling you this up front because if you disagree with it, this will be a frustrating job.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We don't hire based on pedigree.</strong> Logos and school names are weak evidence. What someone has actually done, and what they can demonstrate now, is strong evidence. We design our loops accordingly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We hire for evidence, not affinity.</strong> "Culture fit" that means "reminds me of me" is how companies get homogeneous and slow. We assess against explicit behaviours tied to how we work, and we write down what we saw.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Speed and rigour are not in tension.</strong> Slow processes are usually a symptom of unclear thinking about the role, not of high standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A no should be as clear as a yes.</strong> To the candidate, and internally.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Some of us came from well-known companies.</strong> That's context, not criteria. It isn't why we're here and it won't be why you are. We celebrate everyone's achievements and want to create an environment where diversity of thought and experience of a collective whole makes this place exceptional and lasting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Recruiters are operators, not order-takers.</strong> If you think a role is wrongly scoped, badly levelled, or shouldn't be open at all, you're expected to say so.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>What we're looking for</strong></h1><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years in full-cycle recruiting, with meaningful time in-house at a high-growth company. You've hired in an environment with real ambiguity, not just real volume.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrable depth in either GTM or technical hiring — you can talk through searches you've run, what made them hard, and what you'd do differently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuinely strong sourcing. Not "I partner with a sourcing team." You find people yourself, and you write outreach that people reply to because it's obviously written by a human who read something.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort operating without infrastructure. No playbook, no SDR equivalent, limited tooling to start.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The judgement and directness to challenge senior stakeholders, and the credibility to be listened to when you do.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A bias to start. You see the gap and close it before anyone asks you to.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent written English and a real feel for language. Everything you write is a piece of our employer brand.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Low ego, high ownership. No job is too big or too small — you'll design an assessment framework in the morning and chase a scheduling conflict in the afternoon.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in Paris, London or New York.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ideal, but not required:</strong> experience hiring in AI or developer-facing companies; experience building or improving a hiring process rather than inheriting one; multi-market hiring across Europe and the US.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>You'll be using AI to do this job — properly</strong></h1><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We build the AI operating system that companies use to rewire their work. We expect our own team to be the sharpest possible example of that.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll build and run your own Dust agents: market maps, candidate research, interview debrief synthesis, competitive intelligence on where talent is moving. Not as a side project — as how the job gets done. You don't need to have done this before, but you do need to be the kind of person who is genuinely excited to, rather than politely tolerant of it.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll also be one of our most credible internal sources of feedback on the product, because you'll be a heavy user of it every day.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>Location</strong></h1><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is based in Paris, London or New York, and we'd love you to spend real time in the office with the team. A lot of the best things about building at Dust happen because people are in the same room: the energy, the fast decisions, the unexpected conversation that unlocks a hard problem.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We hire people with strong judgement and extend that trust to how they manage their time.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>Our process</strong></h1><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We'll tell you the full loop up front, keep it to a small number of stages, and give you a decision quickly. You'll meet the people you'd work with, not a panel of proxies. Expect at least one stage where you work through a real hiring problem with us rather than describing a past one.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you don't check every box, apply anyway. We're more interested in your potential and how you think than a perfect match to a checklist.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please send your application and resume in English.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Location</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're prioritizing building our team with an in-person culture at our offices in Paris, London, San Francisco, and New York because we value the magic that happens when talented people work closely together.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have an office-first culture. Some of the best things about building at Dust are the energy, the fast decisions, and the unexpected conversations that unlock a hard problem, which happen because we are in the same room. Being together is not a formality, it is how we do our best work, and it is something we actively protect.<br /><br />That said, we hire people with strong judgement and we extend that trust to how they manage their time. When working from home makes more sense for what you need to get done that day, we trust you to make that call.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Why Dust</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The models are powerful enough. What's missing is the product layer where AI meets how companies actually work. That's what we're building: the infrastructure that lets any team turn scattered knowledge and tools into coordinated execution with agents they build, own, and run themselves.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We use Dust ourselves every day. We get to shape how humans and agents collaborate while solving our own problems with the product we ship. That loop is rare, and it's why we move fast.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're excited about defining a new category and want to join a determined team of optimists who focus on users, ship fast, and don't take themselves too seriously, we'd love to talk.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Even if you don't check every box in our requirements, we encourage you to apply. We value diverse perspectives and backgrounds, and we're more interested in your potential and passion than a perfect match to our checklist. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learn how we think and work.</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://blog.dust.tt/a-first-version-of-our-product-constitution/">Our product constitution,</a> <em>a story about our mission</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="break-all font-semibold transition-all duration-200 ease-in-out hover:underline text-highlight hover:text-highlight-400 active:text-highlight-dark" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xIvlRWEXqqw">Your Next Co-Worker Isn’t Human</a>, <strong>Stanislas Polu</strong>, VivaTech 2026. A conversation about AI agents taking on larger parts of work and how teams collaborate with them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="break-all font-semibold transition-all duration-200 ease-in-out hover:underline text-highlight hover:text-highlight-400 active:text-highlight-dark" href="https://www.nasdaq.com/videos/dust">Dust: Gabriel Hubert on Enterprise AI</a>, <strong>Gabriel Hubert</strong>, Nasdaq, published May 7, 2026. On Dust’s approach to enterprise AI and building the company in Europe.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/dust/senior-talent-partner-tech-paris-5757","tags":["Talent"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1794411620},{"slug":"marketing-operations-paris-france-bordeaux-france-lyon-france-marseille-france-biarritz-france-nantes-france-annecy-france-madrid-spain-218664","company_name":"Alan","title":"Marketing Operations","description":"<h2><strong>Health can’t wait</strong>. </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not for symptoms to get worse. Not for a six‑month appointment. Not for a system to catch up. But that’s exactly how healthcare works today. You wait, until you can’t.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Alan exists to end the wait.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Health is a universal right, and we believe this right can only become real when it’s coupled with prevention. We need to stop treating health as something we repair and start treating it as something we build, every day. It’s not solely a question of willpower. It’s the healthcare system itself that needs to work for everyone, in a sustainable way.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">So we are building the<strong> new standard in prevention insurance. </strong>Alan is the first company that integrates insurance, prevention, and care into a single, acclaimed user experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are on an incredible journey to build a <strong>global leading company, with a </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://alan.com/en/careers"><strong><u>unique culture</u></strong></a>. We already partner with 40K+ companies of all sizes, serving more than 1M+ members, and have reached €800M+ in ARR.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prevention as the new norm. That's what we're building with our team of 1000+ people. If it speaks to you: we're hiring across France, Spain, Belgium, and Canada. And beyond.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Marketing Ops is one of Alan's highest-leverage functions.</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">It sits at the intersection of marketing strategy, data, and technology — turning systems into growth engines and ensuring every touchpoint with prospects and members is timely, relevant, and scalable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Alan is growing fast across France, Belgium, Spain, and Canada. But today we're leaving value on the table. On the <strong>prospect side</strong>, we drive more traffic but can't convert it properly: no scoring, no intelligent routing, no nurturing that adapts to buying intent. On the <strong>member side</strong>, messaging is one of our primary touchpoints for engagement, retention, and trust — yet nobody operates it strategically. Personalization stays shallow, communication pressure goes unmonitored, and shipping a message often means filing an engineering ticket.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We need Marketing Ops leaders who can <strong>architect scalable systems</strong>, <strong>operate them strategically</strong>, and <strong>progressively embed AI</strong> into workflows — to raise quality, reduce manual execution, and unlock growth without scaling headcount linearly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>⭐️ The Marketing Ops job ⭐️</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are hiring <strong>two Marketing Operations Managers</strong>, each embedded in a different crew:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth Infrastructure</strong> — focused on prospect acquisition: building a unified lead engine that captures, scores, routes, and nurtures across all channels</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product Platform</strong> — focused on member lifecycle messaging: operating Alan's messaging stack as a scalable service across 1.7M+ profiles</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Both roles share the same DNA: strong marketing ops fundamentals, data fluency, a product mindset, and the ability to be both hands-on and strategic. <strong>Crew placement will be determined based on the candidate's experience, interests, and fit during the hiring process.</strong><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why is this role interesting?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Speed</strong>: marketing, product, and sales teams ship campaigns and messages confidently — Marketing Ops turns bottlenecks into force multipliers across every crew</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Trust</strong>: clean data, governed attributes, proper segmentation, and enforced rules mean the right person gets the right message at the right time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Scale</strong>: as we grow to millions of members across multiple countries, we need operators who keep our platforms clean and the user experience protected — without scaling headcount linearly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI at the frontier</strong>: this isn't a maintenance role — you'll identify high-priority use cases for AI agents, train and refine them to a senior marketer's quality bar, and drive real adoption</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What will you do with us?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll be a partnership with marketers — not a service desk. You'll partner closely with engineers, data, designers, and cross-functional stakeholders (PMMs, sales, growth, product) within a PM-Tech duo crew model.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regardless of crew, you will own a core set of capabilities:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Marketing Automation &amp; CRM</strong>: own and optimize our marketing stack (<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Customer.io">Customer.io</a>, CRM integrations); build automations that enable marketers to launch campaigns independently, at scale, across all geos</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data Model &amp; Governance</strong>: maintain CRM data quality, attribute/event design, and database hygiene as a sustained practice</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Segmentation &amp; Lifecycle Design</strong>: design and maintain lifecycle stages, segmentation logic, routing rules, and re-engagement flows across multiple audiences and geos</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nurturing Infrastructure</strong>: own the nurturing stack and campaign processes; make launches autonomous and compliant</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-First Operations</strong>: identify, build, and refine AI agents for email copywriting, lead scoring, next-best-action recommendations, and content generation — making marketers AI-powered, not replacing them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Performance Monitoring</strong>: track the full funnel from first touchpoint to conversion; identify leakage and prioritize from data</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Documentation &amp; Enablement</strong>: create playbooks, train teams on tools and processes, reduce the marginal cost of new campaigns</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Then, depending on your crew:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth Infrastructure</strong> — you'll build a unified lead engine (no more tool-by-tool silos), design lead scoring and routing models, crack multi-channel activation (email, WhatsApp, Voice AI), build AI agents that pre-qualify and enrich leads, and maintain a live feedback loop with BDRs, AEs, and Inbound Sales.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product Platform</strong> — you'll operate <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Customer.io">Customer.io</a> and back-end triggered emails as one governed system, monitor communication pressure and enforce channel rules, define and enforce recipient lifecycle paths, drive 100% Design Studio adoption, and co-own outbound messaging strategy with PMMs and product teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>By your first year, we'll know it worked when:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least one AI agent is in production on a key use case (email nurturing, lead categorization, content generation), with a second scoped or live, and adoption is real</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Any marketer or product Alaner can launch a campaign or ship a message without bottlenecking through ops or engineering</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CRM data model, attributes, and segments are properly owned, documented, and clean — the data we see is data we can act on</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every contact has a documented path through our messaging — segmentation is sharp, messaging is relevant, and pressure is monitored</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Marketing's contribution to acquisition and engagement is visible and quantifiable, from first touch to conversion</p></li></ul><h1><br />⭐️ Is it you we are looking for? ⭐️</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />You'll be a great fit for this opportunity if you:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have <strong>5+ years</strong> in Marketing operations, growth ops, CRM ops, lifecycle marketing, or lead generation in a tech environment (B2B, B2C, or B2B2C)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have <strong>hands-on experience managing marketing automation platforms at scale</strong> (<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Customer.io">Customer.io</a>, Braze, Iterable, HubSpot, Marketo, Pardot, Salesforce, or equivalent)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have a <strong>strong understanding of CRM data models</strong> — attribute/event design and data hygiene as a sustained practice</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Can <strong>frame and implement processes</strong> for lead scoring, nurturing, segmentation, and personalization</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have a <strong>product knack</strong>: you can define what's not working, identify what to build next, and see problems as opportunities to bring more value</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring <strong>data fluency and analytical rigor</strong>: you read platform and campaign data, surface anomalies, and draw business insights</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Can <strong>be both hands-on and think strategically</strong> — you drive the big picture while staying close to execution</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have <strong>strong stakeholder management skills</strong> — you'll partner daily with engineering, product, sales, and marketing teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Can <strong>manage multiple projects simultaneously</strong> in a fast-moving environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate with <strong>excellent written and spoken English</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are <strong>impact-driven</strong> with a strong bias towards improving processes</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For this opportunity, we are aiming to hire within the C0-D <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="postings-link" href="https://alan.com/en/careers/a/salary-equity">level range</a>.<br /></p><h1>🙌   <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="postings-link" href="https://alan.com/about/life-at-alan/a/perks">Perks &amp; Benefits</a></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Alan, we believe that <strong>being in good health is a basic need,</strong> and it starts with our employees. This is why Alaners are provided with a stimulating environment and perks ensuring they are <strong>happy, efficient and spend only high-quality time</strong> with co-workers. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Therefore, we offer:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fair rewards</strong>. Generous equity packages complement your base salary, <em>for permanent contracts only.</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexible office with hybrid setup</strong>. Amazing office space at our <strong>Paris</strong> HQ or sponsored co-working hubs in <strong>Bordeaux, Lyon, Marseille, Nantes, Biarritz, Annecy, Brussels, Madrid or Barcelona.</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>All the tools you need</strong>. Top of the range equipment: Macbook Air, keyboard, laptop stand, monitor, and Bose noise-canceling headphones.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexible vacation policy and flexible working hours</strong>. Organize your time as you wish.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Delightful healthcare insurance:</strong> Extremely comprehensive health insurance - 100% for you and your children, 90-100% for partners depending on your country<em> (permanent contracts only).</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Transport</strong>. Generous transit benefit</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning &amp; Training opportunities</strong>. A highly flexible training policy free books and budget to attend and speak at conferences if the opportunity arises.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Personal growth through coaching</strong>: At Alan, coaching isn't just a perk - it's core to who we are. Every Alaner is paired with a dedicated coach from day one, who helps maximize their impact, nurture engagement, and navigate Alan's values to develop their full potential.<strong> </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="notion-link-token notion-focusable-token notion-enable-hover" href="https://alan.com/en/blog/discover-alan/a/alan-culture-excellence-through-coaching"><strong>Learn more about our coaching culture</strong></a><strong>.</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Parental leave</strong>. Extended parental leave for all new parents, <em>for permanent contracts only.</em></p></li></ul><p style="min-hei