énierie Structures"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Sallanches, Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes, France","created_at":1794411085},{"slug":"principal-product-manager-acute-care-ct-paris-357605","company_name":"DeepHealth","title":"Principal Product Manager, Acute Care CT","description":"<p style="text-align:start;">The Principal Product Manager, Acute Care CT owns the DeepHealth Acute Care CT Suite end to end, with primary accountability for what to build and shared accountability for getting it shipped. DeepHealth is building the Acute Care CT Suite from the ground up to cover detection, care coordination, and reporting for emergency CT, starting with head CT and expanding to chest and abdomen, where minutes saved in stroke, bleeds, and trauma directly affect patient outcomes. The Principal Product Manager, Acute Care CT shapes the suite from day one: owning the roadmap, translating clinical needs into ML and product work, and driving cross-functional delivery on a subset of the suite from data through customer activation. The role does not write code or own technical software design.</p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Essential Duties and Responsibilities</p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Product Strategy and Roadmap</p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;">Own the Acute Care CT Suite roadmap and define what to build, defer, or stop based on evidence.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Define suite scope across pathology detection modules, software capabilities such as alerting and care coordination, and comprehensive draft reporting.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Work with emergency radiologists and neuro/stroke teams to distinguish stated requests from real clinical needs, including time-to-treatment, triage, missed findings, and care coordination.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Translate clinical problems into ML work and 