&lt;p&gt;At SentinelOne, we are driven by a clear purpose: to give the advantage to those who secure our future. As AI reshapes how organizations build, operate, and innovate, the responsibility to protect them becomes more critical than ever. When you join SentinelOne, your work helps protect global enterprises, critical infrastructure, and the technologies shaping tomorrow. If you are motivated by meaningful challenges and want your impact to be real, measurable, and global, you will find purpose here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Us&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SentinelOne is a company at the intersection of AI and security, pioneering a new operating model for cybersecurity. Our AI-native platform unifies protection across endpoint, cloud, identity, data, and AI systems to deliver autonomous detection and response with clarity and speed. By combining real-time analytics, intelligent automation, and a unified data foundation, we reduce noise, simplify complexity, and empower security teams to focus on what truly matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our teams are builders, problem-solvers, and innovators committed to shaping the future of security. If you are excited to solve hard problems alongside talented, mission-driven people, we invite you to help us build a safer future for humanity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Are We Looking For?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for people who are relentlessly curious and committed to continuous learning. AI is reshaping every function across our business, and we enable every team member, regardless of role or level, to build fluency in AI tools and concepts. Those who thrive here actively seek out new solutions, experiment thoughtfully, and apply what they learn to drive better, faster, smarter outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a Sr. Channel Account Executive, you will be tasked with managing an assigned group of focus partners in the French region where we are rapidly growing our presence and revenues. This role will report into the Senior Director, Channels SEUR. You will manage existing and grow new national focus partners that will allow better market and vertical sales and support coverage&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What will you do?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Primary responsibilities include&lt;strong&gt;: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and manage an effective channel strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increase Partner Generated revenues and Partner Initiated Deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage existing and grow new national focus partners that will allow better market and vertical sales and support coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute account mapping, meetings and demand generation activities with other SentinelOne staff and partners to qualify target accounts and opportunities that will lead to Partner Initiated Deals and POCs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate monthly, quarterly and yearly planning of sales activities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Enablement sessions to train our focus partners to ensure we have self-sufficient partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build up strong relationships with relevant decision makers and key persons within partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support marketing plans and coordination of marketing activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Skills and Knowledge Will You Bring?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ideal candidates will have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of high-tech channel sales experience in an enterprise sales environment, with experience of both resell and MSSP sales motion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track-record of driving continued partner growth and revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of and network within leading French VAR partners&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understands business models of channel partners and knows how to build in our solutions and offerings into Partner offerings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of the cyber security or similar space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Metrics driven and accountable - takes ownership and responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can work in a fast paced, start-up environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great relation and reputation with key partners in assigned region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to present in front of a bigger audience and to host events with and for partners and end-customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to identify and initiate deals with partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to work on deals and close them with a partner in close sync with SentinelOne Account Teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent French and English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent work experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why us?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is redefining how the world operates and rewriting the rules of security in real time, and SentinelOne was built for this moment. From day one, we architected an AI-native platform designed to operate at machine speed, not as an add-on to legacy systems but as the foundation itself. If you want to build where innovation and impact move together, this is that place.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We invest in our Sentinels with comprehensive, competitive benefits designed to support you and your family:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity &amp;amp; Rewards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Restricted Stock Units (RSUs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Stock Purchase Plan (ESPP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Time Off &amp;amp; Wellbeing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive leave benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gender-neutral parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Insurance &amp;amp; Financial Security&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical and insurance benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Disability insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Program (EAP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Perks &amp;amp; Flexibility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global home office allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mobile phone reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work-from-home allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;SentinelOne is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, gender (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, or other applicable legally protected characteristics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;SentinelOne participates in the E-Verify Program for all U.S. based roles.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;To learn more about how we use AI in our hiring process, please review our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://assets.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt53c99b43892c2378/bltca86b3b84e902400/AI-in-Hiring-SentinelOne.pdf&quot;&gt;AI in Hiring Candidate Disclosure&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/sentinellabs/sr-channel-account-executive-415135","tags":["42300 Channel Sales - EMEA"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1794390917},{"slug":"secops-engineer-paris-61239","company_name":"Signal Processing Engineer (RF Processing & Analytics)","title":"SecOps Engineer","description":"<h3><strong>About Us</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Harmattan AI is a next-generation defense prime building autonomous and scalable defense systems. Following the close of a $200M Series B, valuing the company at $1.4 billion, we are expanding our teams and capabilities to deliver mission-critical systems to allied forces.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work is guided by clear values: building technologies with real-world impact, pursuing excellence in everything we do, setting ambitious goals, and taking on the hardest technical challenges. We operate in a demanding environment where rigor, ownership, and execution are expected.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>About the Role</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">As SecOps Engineer, you join our IT &amp; Cyber team in Paris to protect Harmattan AI’s infrastructure and intellectual property as we scale. You work closely with the security, IT, infrastructure and tooling teams to meet the cyber standards our defense customers expect. You build, automate and continuously improve the tools that detect, respond to and prevent threats, with real autonomy over your scope.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and deliver security engineering projects across cloud, IT and DevSecOps environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Secure our SaaS and PaaS environments through hardened configurations, identity governance and deep-stack visibility.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Handle SOC alerts and lead incident response, including proactive threat hunting and digital forensics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage our MSSP/SOC providers and continuously improve detection rules.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive vulnerability remediation in partnership with the IT and infrastructure teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and audit the technical controls required for advanced certifications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build security tools and use AI to automate routine tasks and streamline operations.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Candidate Requirements</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Degree in Computer Science or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Around 5 years of experience in cybersecurity, IT systems or cloud administration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid skills in at least two of: IT security, security monitoring and incident response, cloud security, AI security.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience going through a security certification process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on approach to building tools and automating your own work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Autonomous, proactive and solution-oriented, with strong curiosity for new stacks and a drive to learn.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Start-up or scale-up experience is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent written and verbal communication, comfortable working with profiles from junior engineers to senior executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong alignment with Harmattan AI’s mission and readiness to go the extra mile in a fast-paced, high-pressure environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in English required.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We look forward to hearing how you can help shape the future of autonomous defense systems at Harmattan AI.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/signal-processing-engineer-rf-processing-analytics/secops-engineer-paris-61239","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1794390014},{"slug":"devops-core-platform-paris-148388","company_name":"Signal Processing Engineer (RF Processing & Analytics)","title":"DevOps, Core Platform","description":"<h3><strong>About Us</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Harmattan AI is a next-generation defense prime building autonomous and scalable defense systems. Following the close of a $200M Series B, valuing the company at $1.4 billion, we are expanding our teams and capabilities to deliver mission-critical systems to allied forces.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work is guided by clear values: building technologies with real-world impact, pursuing excellence in everything we do, setting ambitious goals, and taking on the hardest technical challenges. We operate in a demanding environment where rigor, ownership, and execution are expected.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About the role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are building software infrastructure to power AI development and delivery for operational use cases in defense. Our software needs to run in customers' data centers, on their hardware, often with no internet connection. You will own the continuous deployment of our software in these environments. That covers installations, upgrades with no downtime, and keeping track of dependencies between the services that make up the software.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role involves hands-on coding. You will join the core platform team, with broad ownership and a direct effect on real defense deployments.</p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Delivery:</strong> Take a change from a commit in CI to a running system on a customer site, and keep every step repeatable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Safe upgrades:</strong> Roll out upgrades step by step with no downtime, watch the system as it changes, and stop and alert the team automatically when something goes wrong.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Disconnected sites:</strong> Make installs and upgrades work with no internet, using signed, self-contained packages.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Release checks:</strong> Work on the release system that checks that all our services work together, in CI and at release time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaboration:</strong> Work with platform architects and developers so every new service is easy to package, deploy and upgrade. Work with our forward deployed engineers, who install and run the software at customer sites, so the same tools run in development and at the customer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Documentation:</strong> Write the procedures that a person at a customer site can follow without our help.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth:</strong> Make it easier and faster for our engineers to ship changes to customer sites.</p></li></ul><h2>Candidate requirements</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience:</strong> Several years of backend or infrastructure engineering, ideally on a product with many services and 