e MS-Office-Kenntnisse, SAP von Vorteil</li><li>Sehr gute Deutsch- und Englischkenntnisse</li><li>Kenntnisse über Zertifizierungsprozesse, insbesondere für Umweltzeichen, von Vorteil</li><li>Bereitschaft zu gelegentlichen Geschäftsreisen</li></ul><p><strong>Ihre Chance:</strong></p><ul><li>Flexible Arbeitszeitmodelle</li><li>Mitarbeitergeschenke</li><li>Homeoffice</li><li>Gleitzeit</li><li>Mitarbeiterevents</li><li>Interne / Externe Weiterbildung</li><li>Ferien</li><li>Kostenlose Parkplätze</li><li>Betriebliche Altersvorsorge</li><li>Kostenloser Kaffee</li><li>Feiertage</li><li>Arbeitsplatz</li><li>Wir bieten Ihnen ein interessantes Aufgabengebiet in einem innovativen und wachstumsorientierten Unternehmen. Wenn Sie gerne selbständig und eigenverantwortlich arbeiten, kurze Entscheidungswege schätzen und Freude an dieser spannenden Tätigkeit haben, freuen wir uns auf Ihre Bewerbungsunterlagen.</li></ul><p>Sifloor AG</p><p>Elisabetta Bisaro, Leiterin ----- | Tel. direkt 041 624 48 97</p><p>Bitte stellen Sie uns mit Ihrem Lebenslauf auch Ihre <strong>Zeugnisse und Diplome</strong> zu. Herzlichen Dank vorab!</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/twojobs/projektmanager-fe-sursee-420304","tags":["Project Management"],"job_types":["Unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag","teamleitung"],"location":"Sursee","created_at":1794477747},{"slug":"principal-design-engineer-mechanical-equipment-80-100-zurich-483998","company_name":"Climeworks","title":"Principal Design Engineer - Mechanical Equipment (80-100%)","description":"<p class="MsoNormal"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Lead technically by doing.</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#121317">Join our Design Engineering team as a highly experienced individual contributor. You will take on challenging mechanical design problems yourself, from concepts and CAD models to manufacturing drawings, prototypes and tested hardware, while helping the wider team make strong technical decisions.&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#121317">As a Principal Design Engineer, you are a hands-on member of our Design Engineering team, designing Climeworks’ CO2 collectors, the heart of our direct air capture plant. Improving how they perform, are manufactured and scale is central to the future success of DAC.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Mechanical concept &amp; product design:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You personally turn new concepts into robust physical products: developing mechanical concepts, creating CAD models, designing components and complete collector assemblies, producing manufacturing drawings, and supporting hardware through fabrication, assembly and testing.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Engineering problem-solving &amp; risk reduction:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Your experience helps you find the right solutions faster, anticipate problems early and reduce risk before issues reach manufacturing or testing.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">CO2 collector design:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You take mechanical systems from requirements and concepts through to detailed, manufacturable designs. You develop solutions, perform engineering calculations and make the decisions needed to create robust industrial hardware.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">First-principles engineering:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You use experience and first-principles reasoning to identify risks early, evaluate alternatives quickly and converge on simple, robust solutions. You apply calculations, tolerance analysis, design reviews and testing to reduce uncertainty.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Own design from concept to commercialisation:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You work directly in SolidWorks to create and modify parts, assemblies and system layouts. You manage complex interfaces, packaging constraints and design changes so the complete system works together. You produce and maintain high-quality 2D manufacturing drawings, including appropriate GD&amp;T, tolerances, materials, finishes and manufacturing requirements.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Prototype fabrication, assembly &amp; testing:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You stay closely involved after the CAD work is complete. You support prototype fabrication, assembly and testing, investigate issues and incorporate the learning back into the design.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Technical leadership &amp; design reviews:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You act as a senior technical reference for the team, supporting the Design Engineering line manager with design reviews, engineering standards and approval of critical designs. You support the extended team with technical judgement on complex mechanical design decisions, help maintain strong engineering practices and share your experience through everyday collaboration, mentoring and constructive challenge.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Cross-functional engineering collaboration:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You work with manufacturing, testing, process engineering, procurement, suppliers and other engineering disciplines to ensure mechanical designs work as part of the complete product. You integrate external design resources where needed.</span></p></li></ul> <br> <p class="MsoNormal"><strong><span style="color:#121317">What makes you stand out</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#121317">Your experience makes your engineering more effective: you spot promising solutions early, expose weak points before they become expensive, and deliver designs that are clear, manufacturable and ready to perform in the real world.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p class="paragraph"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Mechanical Design Experience</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: You bring 15+ years of hands-on mechanical design experience, ideally developing complex industrial equipment from concept through manufacture, assembly and testing.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p class="paragraph"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Sheet Metal Design &amp; Manufacturing</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: You have deep practical experience designing sheet-metal parts, structures and assemblies for manufacture at scale. You understand bending, welding and joining methods, forming, tolerances, material and thickness selection, and how design choices affect tooling, cost, assembly and quality.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p class="paragraph"><strong><span style="color:#121317">CAD &amp; Drawings</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: You are an expert SolidWorks user and remain hands-on with CAD. You personally create high-quality manufacturing drawings and are confident with GD&amp;T and tolerance chains.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p class="paragraph"><strong><span style="color:#121317">System Design &amp; Engineering Judgement: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">You have experience designing from components and mechanisms through subsystems, interfaces and complex assemblies. You understand how decisions at one level affect the complete collector and can balance structures, airflow, movement, sealing, process interfaces, manufacturability, reliability and cost to arrive at robust solutions.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p class="paragraph"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Manufacturing &amp; DFMA</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: You have strong knowledge of machined parts, welded structures, materials and manufacturing processes, and apply DFMA to create robust, cost-effective designs.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p class="paragraph"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Collaboration &amp; Technical Leadership</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: You work effectively with engineers, technicians, manufacturers and suppliers. You share your experience, challenge constructively and help others make better technical decisions.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p class="paragraph"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Education:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You have a Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Mechanical Engineering or similar.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong><span style="color:#121317">This job is not for you, if…</span></strong></p><ul><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst"><span style="color:#121317">you mainly want to manage people or projects.</span></p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle"><span style="color:#121317"> you mainly do simulation, concept work or system-level engineering without your own CAD work.</span></p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast"><span style="color:#121317">you have no experience with sheet metal, welded structures or manufacturing at scale.</span></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW212189085 BCX8" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW212189085 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Our promis