job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Bern, Berne, Switzerland","created_at":1794141082},{"slug":"senior-network-engineer-zurich-142802","company_name":"SwissPeak Partners GmbH","title":"Senior Network Engineer","description":"<p style="text-align:start;">Our client is an established, family-owned industrial technology company headquartered near Zurich. Its systems run at customer sites in more than 60 countries. To keep them reachable and secure, it needs someone who can build and run the networks behind them, and who is comfortable intervening and troubleshooting when a customer's connection goes down.<br></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul><li><p>Set up, run and troubleshoot site-to-site and remote-access VPNs to customer sites (IPsec, OpenVPN)</p></li><li><p>Configure and maintain firewalls (Fortinet, OPNsense and others)</p></li><li><p>Design and implement networks at customer sites: switching, routing, VLANs, WLAN</p></li><li><p>Find and fix network problems together with customers and colleagues around the world, remotely or on site</p></li><li><p>Install and roll out software on Windows and Linux systems</p></li><li><p>Build and maintain the internal test and lab networks</p></li><li><p>Keep network documentation clear and up to date, and help improve how the team works</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>What you bring</strong></p><ul><li><p>A completed IT or electrical engineering education (EFZ with further training, HF, FH or equivalent)</p></li><li><p>At least three years of hands-on experience in network or system engineering</p></li><li><p>Solid knowledge of TCP/IP, routing, switching and firewalls</p></li><li><p>Real experience with VPNs, ideally IPsec and OpenVPN</p></li><li><p>Working knowledge of Windows Server</p></li><li><p>A calm, customer-focused way of solving problems, including under pressure</p></li><li><p>Fluent German and English</p></li><li><p>Willingness to travel occasionally for on-site work</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul><li><p>Linux administration</p></li><li><p>Scripting or automation (Python, Bash)</p></li><li><p>Certifications such as CCNA/CCNP or Fortinet NSE</p></li><li><p>A background in network or cyber security</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>What's on offer</strong></p><ul><li><p>Room to shape the role and how things are done</p></li><li><p>Flexible working model with home office (up to 60%) </p></li><li><p>Individual training and certification budget</p></li><li><p>Comprehensive social benefits</p></li><li><p>A long-term position in a stable, family-owned company</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/swisspeak-partners-gmbh/senior-network-engineer-zurich-142802","tags":["Infrastructure & DevOps"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Zurich, Zürich, Switzerland","created_at":1794141082},{"slug":"senior-java-angular-engineer-zurich-433887","company_name":"SwissPeak Partners GmbH","title":"Senior Java/Angular Engineer","description":"<p>For a renowned Swiss bank in Zurich, we are looking for an experienced Java/Angular engineer. In a newly built DevOps team you help develop the new platform for digital onboarding and product opening and run its services. </p><h3>Your tasks</h3><ol><li><p>Build, develop and operate services in the DevOps team</p></li><li><p>Verify solutions against internal and external security standards</p></li><li><p>Improve operating processes and contribute to service design and architecture</p></li><li><p>Advise the business on feasibility and options, working closely with the product owner, business engineers and architecture</p></li><li><p>Depending on the position, introduce Camunda 8 and enable the team</p></li></ol><h3>Your profile</h3><ol><li><p>German at C1 level or higher, the project language is German. Understanding of Swiss German is expected. English at B2 level</p></li><li><p>Experience in client onboarding, digital product closings or client lifecycle management in finance within the last three years</p></li><li><p>Very good Java and Angular skills with Spring, JPA/Hibernate, Maven and SQL with PostgreSQL</p></li><li><p>Experience with Scrum or Kanban and a DevOps mindset</p></li><li><p>Degree in computer science or equivalent professional experience</p></li></ol><h3>Nice to have</h3><ol><li><p>Camunda 8, including process design and implementation</p></li><li><p>Kotlin, Kubernetes with AKS, Docker</p></li><li><p>Git, IntelliJ, Jenkins, Sonar, Jira</p></li></ol><h3></h3><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/swisspeak-partners-gmbh/senior-java-angular-engineer-zurich-433887","tags":[],"job_types":["Experienced","contract"],"location":"Zurich, Zürich, Switzerland","created_at":1794141082},{"slug":"business-engineer-investment-and-pension-zurich-66663","company_name":"SwissPeak Partners GmbH","title":"Business Engineer Investment and Pension","description":"<p>For a renowned Swiss bank in Zurich, we are looking for an experienced business engineer for digital investment and pension solutions. Topics include pillar 3a, vested benefits, mandate and portfolio fund solutions, and quote simulation in occupational pension.</p><h3>Your tasks</h3><ol><li><p>Customer-centred requirements analysis, capture as-is and to-be processes</p></li><li><p>Specify features and stories, create GUI prototypes with UX and UI</p></li><li><p>Run workshops and refinements with the business, product management and IT</p></li><li><p>Identify and eliminate manual interfaces and media breaks in the to-be process</p></li><li><p>Support implementation, testing and acceptance of features</p></li></ol><h3>Your profile</h3><ol><li><p>German at C2 level, the project language is German. Understanding of Swiss German is expected</p></li><li><p>At least five years of business engineering or business analysis at a bank, financial services provider or insurer</p></li><li><p>Experience with digital investment platforms, pension or advisory solutions</p></li><li><p>BPMN, use cases, user stories and story maps</p></li><li><p>Agile way of working, ideally SAFe</p></li><li><p>Degree in business administration, banking and finance or business informatics</p></li></ol><h3>Nice to have</h3><ol><li><p>Figma, Jira and Confluence</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of Swiss occupational pension (BVG, KTG, UVG, UVGZ)</p></li><li><p>Mandate and portfolio fund solutions at large banks</p></li></ol><h3></h3><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/swisspeak-partners-gmbh/business-engineer-investment-and-pension-zurich-66663","tags":["Projectlead & Business Analyst"],"job_types":["Experienced","contract"],"location":"Zurich, Zürich, Switzerland","created_at":1794141082},{"slug":"anti-financial-crime-analyst-dutch-german-speaker-amsterdam-224950","company_name":"Qonto","title":"Anti-Financial Crime Analyst - Dutch & German Speaker","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us as an Anti-Financial Crime Analyst (DE) in our Amsterdam office to investigate and report suspicious activities, ensuring Qonto's compliance with German AML/CFT regulations. You'll join our Anti-Financial Crime team and work closely with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ludmi%C5%82a-moroniewicz-5424a410a/">Ludmila Moroniewicz</a>, our Lead Anti-Financial Crime Germany &amp; CDD, to protect our growing German client base from financial crime risks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">➡️<strong> What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Investigate and report:</strong> Perform enhanced investigations on suspicious client activities and issue Suspicious Transaction Reports (STR) to the German FIU when necessary.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ensure reporting quality:</strong> Detect and describe patterns on investigated accounts to ensure regulatory reports meet the highest standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Handle team escalations:</strong> Investigate cases escalated by the transaction monitoring team, assess risk, and recommend next steps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strengthen the AFC framework:</strong> Contribute to improving investigation processes and documentation standards as Qonto's German operations scale.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ What we're looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AML/Financial Crime experience:</strong> You have first experience in AML, Financial Crime, or Compliance — ideally in fintech or banking. You've handled real cases, not just studied the theory.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Analytical rigor:</strong> You have a logical mind and can analyze complex datasets, spot errors, and build well-reasoned investigation conclusions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Quality and throughput:</strong> You deliver high-quality work while managing multiple cases in parallel — you know how to prioritise without cutting corners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Language proficiency:</strong> Fluency in English, Dutch and German is required for this role.<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ What we can offer you</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real investigative work:</strong> You'll handle STRs, enhanced due diligence, and escalation reviews — not back-office monitoring. The cases are complex and the stakes are real.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A market you'll help build:</strong> Qonto's German AFC processes were built from scratch. You'll contribute to an operation that's still being shaped, not just maintained.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Investigative culture:</strong> The team values logical thinking and curiosity — understanding the <em>why</em> behind a transaction matters more than ticking a checklist.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ Your future manager</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your manager will be <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ludmi%C5%82a-moroniewicz-5424a410a/">Ludmila Moroniewicz</a>, our Lead Anti-Financial Crime Germany &amp; CDD.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Her path?</strong> 9 years in Money Laundering prevention in fintech — from KYC/KYB roles to AFC Lead, reporting directly to the MLRO of Qonto's German branch. She contributed to launching Qonto's operations in Germany and built the Financial Crime processes for the German market from scratch. Her Global CDD Expert role gave her an overview of KYC/KYB processes across all Qonto markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What does she bring to the team?</strong> A hands-on leadership style that fosters continuous learning and professional growth. She knows the German regulatory landscape inside out and gives her team the autonomy to own their investigations.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>[DIVERSITY]</strong> <em>At Qonto, we understand that true diversity isn’t just about ticking boxes on a hiring checklist. Apply regardless of the boxes you tick - who knows? You may have the missing piece of the puzzle we’ve been searching for all along.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>[HIRING PROCESS DURATION]</strong> <em>On average, <strong>our hiring process lasts 20 working days. </strong>More information on our candidate journey </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://qonto.com/en/careers/candidate-journey"><em><strong><u>here</u></strong></em></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>[DATA RETENTION]</strong> <em>By applying, you agree that Qonto processes your personal data to assess your application. Your data is kept for up to 2 years in our candidate pool. Read our </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://qonto.com/en/legal-documents/privacy-notice"><em><u>Privacy Notice</u></em></a><em> for full details.</em></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/qonto/anti-financial-crime-analyst-dutch-german-speaker-amsterdam-224950","tags":["Finance","Legal","Risk & Compliance","People & Strat"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam, Netherlands","created_at":1794336040},{"slug":"ai-builder-amsterdam-350278","company_name":"Contentoo","title":"AI Builder","description":"<h2>The short version</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plenty of companies are still running AI pilots. We moved past that a while ago: AI agents and human experts create, localise, check and refresh content for global B2B brands every day, across markets and languages. The next question is a harder one: not how to make content, but which content a client should make at all. That's where you come in.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As an AI Builder, you work on both sides of that. About half your time goes to bringing new clients live. The rest goes to building the intelligence that tells each client what to make next: where competitors outrank them, which pages are losing ground and need a refresh, which topics are an opening nobody has claimed yet, and whether they show up when people ask ChatGPT or Google instead of searching.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We've built our own CRM; our teams work with agents that do everything from setting up a tailor-made demo for a prospect to preparing sales calls and routing client feedback to the right person, and people across the company build their own tools. If you want to do serious work with AI, this is a good place for it. Everyone here is already building.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What Contentoo does</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Most content tools make the client the editor. Most agencies make them the project manager. We'd rather make them the approver: they brief, review, and approve, and we run everything in between, inside their own workflow and tools. That makes us a product with a large service layer, sitting where SaaS, service and AI overlap.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">None of that works without good foundations, so that's where we start. Before any agent runs, we capture what makes a client's content theirs: strategy, tone, terminology, compliance rules and hero pieces, per language and market, confirmed by the client. Every agent, expert and signal draws on that brand context. Skip it, and you get generic content, faster.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">There's no shortage of software that tells a client what to write. The difference is that we get those foundations right first and then actually do the work. We've been doing that for ten years: 300+ brands, 300,000+ completed projects and 49 languages. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you'll do</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">A suite of Workflows already runs in production, from localisation and creation to brand checks and content refresh. Each one combines AI agents with human experts and works from the client's brand context.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In practice, your week splits two ways. Half of it is implementation: getting new clients live, finding out where their situation is different from the last client's, and building the fix quickly, whether that's a new skill for their agent, a connection to their CMS, or a check only their market needs. Then you make that whole process faster and more automated on our side, so the next client goes live with less hand work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The other half is the layer on top, which we're building right now: brand intelligence. Today most marketing teams guess what to write next. We want every client to know. Their own search data shows which pages are slipping, and a page that slips already gets a one-click refresh. Competitor rankings show where others win the topics the client should own. Strategy gets drafted from search data in each market and confirmed by the client, so every piece has a reason to exist. And every week we ask ChatGPT, Gemini, and Google's AI to answer the questions their buyers ask, to see whether the client is named or a competitor is. Every expert fix and every client comment flows back into the brand context, so the platform gets better with each piece.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What works for one client becomes a feature for all of them. And our own teams are clients too. Sales asks the CRM and the agents for a prospect's history before a call. Anyone in the company can ask Conny, our assistant on top of KIWI, our company knowledge base, how billing works or what a package includes. Product feedback from clients gets sorted and routed to the right owner by an agent. When one of those tools needs to get better, you build that too, with Claude Code, the Claude and GPT APIs, MCP servers and agent skills: whatever does the job.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The team</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You join the Product team under Olivier (CPO) and report to Joost (AI Lead), in our growing AI team. You'll work closely with Jorge (Product Lead), Cesar (Tech Lead) and our development hub in Valencia.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Around you are the Connies: our people in Amsterdam and in our growing Valencia office. Once a month we stop for Success &amp; Drinks, a company update with no slides and lots of energy, where anyone can take the floor to show what they've built. Wins get celebrated in #shoutout, from a sales call that nailed it to the talent team finding the right experts for a client's healthcare content. We play a padel tournament every year, run the city business run together (the ones who don't run come for the drinks afterwards), and take honest feedback seriously enough to train for it. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Who you are</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're a builder who gets energy from seeing a client actually use what you made. Three things come together in you:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Judgement.</strong> You quickly see what's really going on with a client, and you're as credible talking ROI with a CFO as architecture with an engineer.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You build.</strong> You prototype fast and ship, and you're at home with LLM APIs, agents, MCP, skills, and tools like Claude Code. You've built AI tools that real people use, and you can tell us what happened after launch.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands in the mud.</strong> You love being close to clients: fixing what gets in their way, building what solves their next problem, and owning what you ship. Under the hood, it has to work, stay up, and be safe. Your best hours go to the client.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You might come from strategy, product, solutions engineering, or technical implementation. Or you became the AI person at your last company and want a lot more of it. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English is a must; Dutch is a plus. We are looking for someone available 32-40h per week.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>If seeing a client use something you built last week excites you more than perfecting the architecture behind it, you'll love it here. You'd be building on a business that's doing very well, with a large network of expert freelancers behind it: clients, data, and experts from day one, and an operation that keeps running while we scale. If you'd rather start from a blank page, a startup will suit you better. But if you want to make AI fly at scale, this is the place.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you’ll get</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A competitive salary based on experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 vacation days per year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension contribution</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid work environment (great office at the Houthavens, 2-3 days in office, plus remote flexibility)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A small AI team with a mandate to grow: real leadership opportunities, an L&amp;D budget and direct exposure to the MT and founders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Laptop of choice (Mac or HP)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A monthly Alleo budget</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A learning budget</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lunch and a bar in the office. Who doesn’t want a bar in their office?!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A fun, inclusive team, regular company events, boat days, and more</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Why Contentoo, why now</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li>