You are comfortable coding, with the help of AI agents like Claude Code, in multiple languages and eager to learn our tech stack</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are in your final year of a degree in Software Engineering, Computer Science, or a related field and looking for a 6-month full-time internship</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Eager to learn and work in a team of builders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are fluent in English</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>It would be fantastic if you:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have experience with web development or building products in a fast-paced environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have worked on side projects or contributed to open-source communities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are familiar with AI-assisted coding tools and eager to integrate them into your daily workflow.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Life at Doctolib Tech</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our solutions are built on a single fully cloud-native platform that supports web and mobile app interfaces, multiple languages, and is adapted to country and healthcare specialty requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our stack is composed of Rails, TypeScript, Java, Python, Kotlin, Swift, and React Native.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We leverage AI ethically across our products to empower patients and health professionals. Discover our AI vision <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://careers.doctolib.com/ai-careers/">here</a>.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Want to learn more about our tech culture and environment? Visit the</em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://careers.doctolib.com/tech-doctolib/"><em> Doctolib Tech site</em></a><em>.</em></p><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tech masterclasses throughout the internship</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Free breakfast and lunch plan every day on-site</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Up to 2 days of remote work per week</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to the best AI tools for coding and development, along with dedicated training</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Discounted membership to Urban Sports Club</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bike lease scheme with our partner Lease a Bike, 35% price below the market</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reimbursement of public transportation if you live outside the Amsterdam highway ring</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprehensive health insurance, fully covered by Doctolib for employees and their children under the basic plan</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Free mental health and personalised coaching programme with our partner,<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://moka.care/"> Moka.care</a></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our interview process</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coding Game (1h)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recruiter Interview (30 minutes)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Feature Building Interview (1h)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Behavioral Interview (1h)</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Job details</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Internship (6 months)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Amsterdam</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid work setup (up to 2 remote days per week)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Start date: March 2027</p></li></ul><h2><strong>We welcome everyone</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Doctolib, we are committed to improving access to healthcare for everyone. This translates into our recruitment process. We evaluate candidates based solely on qualifications and motivation, without any form of discrimination.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The more diverse ideas are heard, the more our product will truly improve healthcare for all. You are welcome to apply to Doctolib, regardless of your gender, religion, age, sexual orientation, ethnicity, or disability.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To ensure equal opportunities, we invite you to exclude personal information (e.g., pictures, age) from your applications. If you require any accommodation, please let us know for support during the hiring process.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us in building the healthcare we all dream of!</p><h2><strong>Your data privacy</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">All information provided is processed by Doctolib for application management. For data processing details, click here:<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://doctolib.legal/B2C-Privacy-Policy-Career-DE"> Germany</a> |<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://doctolib.legal/B2C-Privacy-Policy-Career-FR"> France</a> |<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://doctolib.legal/B2C-Privacy-Policy-Career-IT"> Italy</a> |<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://doctolib.legal/B2C-Privacy-Policy-Career-COM"> Netherlands</a>. Please contact hr.dataprivacy(at)doctolib.com for inquiries or to exercise your rights.</p><h3><br /><br /></h3><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/doctolib/software-engineer-intern-fullstack-amsterdam-377938","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Intern"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794336039},{"slug":"supply-chain-lead-netherlands-69580","company_name":"Rnrs.solutions","title":"Supply Chain Lead","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Build the supply chain behind technology that is already operating at scale.</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re partnering with a fast-growing defence technology company developing and mass-producing autonomous systems for real-world deployment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a full-cycle hardware business where R&amp;D, engineering, manufacturing and field operations sit close together and where products evolve continuously based on direct operational feedback.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The company is already operating at meaningful scale, with a growing ecosystem spanning UAVs, unmanned ground systems and communication technologies. As production and international operations expand, they are now building a more resilient and scalable electronics supply chain across Europe.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for the Supply Chain Lead to build and own this function.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>The Role:</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reporting directly to the CEO, you’ll take ownership of the electronics supply chain end-to-end from EMS strategy and semiconductor sourcing to BOM resilience, logistics and cross-border operations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not a procurement coordination role or an established function to simply maintain.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll help determine where and how products are manufactured, how critical components are secured, which EMS and semiconductor partners the company builds around, and how the supply chain scales with production.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For someone coming from the European semiconductor, electronics or EMS ecosystem, this is an opportunity to move from owning one part of a mature supply chain to building one with significant autonomy and direct access to decision-makers.<br /></p><h1><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Source and manage EMS partners</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage BOM risk, including allocation, EOL, pre-buys and alternates</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain relationships with semiconductor manufacturers and distributors</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage logistics from suppliers and EMS partners to the company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage logistics to customers in the EU and Ukraine</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage customs and export compliance</p></li></ul><h1><strong>Requirements:</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of experience in electronics supply chain on the OEM or EMS side</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience through a component shortage cycle</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Supplier and distributor relationships you actively use</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of EU customs and dual-use rules</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Highly relevant:</strong> defence, UAV, robotics or other complex electronics environments; hands-on SMT manufacturing experience.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><h1><strong>Why This Role:</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The interesting part is not the title, it’s the level of ownership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re joining at the point where the company needs to turn a fast-moving electronics supply chain into a scalable international function.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/rnrssolutions/supply-chain-lead-netherlands-69580","tags":["External"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Netherlands","created_at":1794336039},{"slug":"hardware-electronics-engineer-uav-leerdam-193959","company_name":"Rnrs.solutions","title":"Hardware Electronics Engineer (UAV)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Details:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Location: Leerdam, Netherlands (hybrid or remote)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employment: full-time or B2B</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Level: Middle / Senior</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're partnering with a defence technology company developing and mass-producing autonomous systems for real-world deployment.<br />This is a full-cycle hardware business where R&amp;D, engineering, manufacturing and field operations sit close together, and where products evolve continuously based on direct operational feedback.<br />The company is already operating at meaningful scale, with a growing ecosystem spanning UAVs, unmanned ground systems and communication technologies. As the product line expands, they're strengthening the hardware team. We're looking for a Hardware Electronics Engineer to join this team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role:</strong><br />You'll design electronics for UAV components, primarily flight controllers and ESCs, and own the full hardware cycle from schematic to production-ready PCB. You'll take boards through layout, manufacturing outputs, DFM with fabs and assembly houses, and into the lab for bring-up and debugging, with your designs going into products that are built at volume and used in the field.<br />For an engineer with a background in power electronics or motor control, this is an opportunity to work on compact, high-current boards where design decisions have direct, visible impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design schematics for flight controllers, ESCs and related UAV electronics: component selection, power stages, MCU circuits, sensors and interfaces</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create multilayer PCB layouts in Altium, including high-current power routing, thermal management and signal integrity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare manufacturing outputs: Gerbers, BOM, pick-and-place, assembly drawings</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the DFM/DFA phase together with PCB fabs and assembly houses</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring up and debug prototypes, and fix issues found in testing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take part in peer design reviews, both giving and receiving feedback</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain design documentation and component libraries</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Requirements:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years of hands-on hardware design experience (schematic and PCB layout)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong working knowledge of Altium Designer</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with multilayer PCBs and power electronics: DC-DC converters, MOSFET stages, current sensing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with microcontroller-based designs (e.g. STM32) and common interfaces: SPI, I2C, UART, CAN</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical understanding of DFM/DFA and work with PCB manufacturers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lab skills: oscilloscope, power supply, multimeter, soldering and rework</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical English sufficient to read datasheets and write documentation</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Would be a plus</strong>: direct experience with drone flight controllers or ESCs (BLDC motor drives, FOC); familiarity with ArduPilot, PX4 or Betaflight hardware ecosystems; EMC/EMI-aware design for compact, high-current boards; design for harsh environments (vibration, temperature); basic Python for test automation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/rnrssolutions/hardware-electronics-engineer-uav-leerdam-193959","tags":["External"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Leerdam, NL","created_at":1794336039},{"slug":"senior-product-engineer-booking-management-amsterdam-30836","company_name":"Wetravel","title":"Senior Product Engineer - Booking Management","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Hi! 👋 I'm <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/srmillington/"><u>Sam</u></a>, Engineering Manager for Team Booking Management at WeTravel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">I joined WeTravel to help simplify how group travel businesses handle payments and bookings. Our Booking Management team owns the journey from the moment a traveler decides to book: checkout flows, order management, tax management, and everything that enables travelers to easily make a reservation and manage it afterwards. Last year alone, over a million travelers booked adventures through our platform! As we streamline and localize our booking experience, I'm looking for engineers who are excited about making complex booking and commerce flows feel simple for our global users.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About WeTravel:</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Think of the most incredible adventures imaginable: trekking to Machu Picchu, cycling through Tuscany, or going on a safari in Kenya. For years, the small businesses and local experts who run these trips have been stuck using messy spreadsheets, countless emails, and complicated payment methods.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">WeTravel is changing that. We build the tools that empower any entrepreneur to launch and grow their own travel business. Our platform makes it simple for organizers to create beautiful trip proposals, securely process payments, and manage their customers, so they can focus on what they do best: creating amazing experiences.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is one of the last great frontiers of travel to come online, and as the category leader, we are at the forefront of this change. <strong>Last year alone, our platform was trusted by 8,000 organizers to lead over a million travelers on adventures in 150+ countries.</strong> Now, we're on an exciting journey to grow from powering $1B to $10B in travel experiences per year.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe that every trip, when done right, can be a force for good - and we're building the engine to make more of that possible.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What's the role:</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will join the Booking Management team to lead critical projects across checkout, order management, tax management, and traveler self-service. Upcoming work includes:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Checkout experience:</strong> streamlining and localizing our checkout flows so travelers in every market can complete a reservation in just a few clicks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Order management:</strong> building the foundational systems for organizers and travelers to view, modify, and manage reservations end-to-end - changes, transfers, cancellations, and everything in between.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Tax management:</strong> expanding our tax capabilities across jurisdictions so organizers can sell compliantly wherever their travelers are.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reliability and structural improvements:</strong> scaling our booking flows to support 10x growth.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you'll do day-to-day:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead booking projects end-to-end: discovery with Product and Customer teams, solution design, build, rollout, monitoring, and incident response.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with the Product team to gain insight into organizer and traveler challenges, building booking experiences that convert and delight.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the reliability of our booking and order management systems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to WeTravel's engineering practices and excellence.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>How we work:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're focused on the impact. We don't subscribe to any one framework or execution ideology, and we adapt based on what's impactful.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're using the latest hardware and constantly on the look out for better tools &amp; ways to work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have AI-first development experience and work with the latest models and agentic dev tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stack: We're developing React/TypeScript, Ruby on Rails and Kotlin Microservices. Our services run on Kubernetes. We also use and love MongoDB, MySQL, Postgres, Snowflake and we're working with the major LLM providers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>You should apply if you have:</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Basic qualifications:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7+ years of product engineering expertise, with 4+ years dedicated to architecting complex e-commerce, booking, or order management systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record within a high-scale consumer checkout, marketplace, travel, or e-commerce platform team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Broad practical expertise in building and troubleshooting production-level checkout and order flows: conversion-critical funnels, pricing and tax calculation, availability and inventory, cancellations, modifications, and refund flows. You possess deeply ingrained expertise in order state machines, multi-step form UX, and the operational tooling that keeps commerce systems running.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong backend mastery in Ruby on Rails, Kotlin, Python, Go, Java, or Node.js with the agility to ramp up on Ruby quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full-stack comfort: you can build the React interface for the booking flows you architect.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep expertise in architecting robust, resilient distributed systems, including order and reservation state machines, idempotency, exactly-once semantics, event-driven architectures, webhooks, and reliable consumer patterns.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct production on-call experience, including authoring post-mortems and leading incident response.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including cross-functional collaboration experience, and the ability to thrive in a distributed, multicultural environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pragmatic adoption of AI tools to optimize your engineering workflow, including the ability to mentor and train others on AI concepts.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical Skills</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong background in cloud infrastructure (AWS/GCP), containerization, and modern CI/CD practices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in handling critical systems with precision: you will handle pricing and tax logic directly within the application layer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bonus: Direct experience with tax engines or multi-jurisdiction tax compliance (VAT, GST, sales tax), or with travel-industry reservation systems.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Preferred qualifications:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience launching or significantly redesigning a checkout or booking flow end-to-end.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building tax calculation or compliance capabilities across multiple jurisdictions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in marketplace or two-sided platform commerce (orders spanning buyers, sellers, and modifications over time).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>You might not be the right fit if you:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your commerce expertise is limited to plugging in off-the-shelf checkout or cart solutions. We need someone who operates deeply beneath that abstraction layer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are hesitant to take full ownership of mission-critical booking flows or participate in the on-call rotation when systems fail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You prioritize greenfield development over the complex challenge of scaling and refining an existing system with significant booking volume.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are looking for a siloed IC position without the need for cross-functional collaboration or product-level discovery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You require a rigid, pre-defined roadmap; we prefer to sharpen our strategy and direction as we scale the team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Why join us?</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solve real commerce problems at real volume: over a million travelers booking adventures in 150+ countries, and growing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make a real impact: you'll help build the operating system for the multi-day group travel industry, empowering thousands of organizers and millions of travelers worldwide.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solve meaningful technical challenges at scale, from designing robust systems to improving real-time user experiences in a complex domain.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be part of building the best engineering team: you'll help shape culture, mentor others, and contribute to high standards of excellence and collaboration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enjoy flexibility and balance, with competitive compensation, generous PTO, and remote-friendly work culture.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Benefits Section</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous "Time to Recharge" policy - enjoy unlimited paid time off to rest, recharge, and show up as your best self.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work remotely for a maximum of 4 weeks per calendar year.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2-week cross-functional onboarding program.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cycle-to-work scheme (Swapfiets subscription) or commuting reimbursement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monday/Thursday team lunches and after-work social events.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Extensive paid family leave.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Three paid volunteer days per year - take time to give back to causes you care about, on us.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cutting-edge equipment and tools to set you up for success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join an international, travel-loving team with a passion for adventure and innovation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to our Booking Marketplace: Book hotels and flights for personal travel at exclusive discounted rates.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Equal Opportunities</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">WeTravel is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. If you're excited about this opportunity and believe you're a good fit, we encourage you to apply and join us in transforming the travel industry!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/wetravel/senior-product-engineer-booking-management-amsterdam-30836","tags":["Engineering & Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794336038},{"slug":"senior-solutions-engineer-amsterdam-487719","company_name":"Wetravel","title":"Senior Solutions Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Behind every unforgettable trip is a travel business that needs its tools to just work. Our Solution Engineering team makes that possible: we connect WeTravel to the way organizers already run their business, so growing from ten trips to a thousand never means drowning in manual work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Senior Solution Engineer, your role spans both pre- and post-sale: from technical evaluation and solution design with high-value prospects, to driving adoption and long-term implementation with existing customers. Every integration you deliver will teach us what to build next, and you’ll turn those lessons into better public interfaces for all our organizers!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About WeTravel</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Think of the most incredible adventures imaginable: trekking to Machu Picchu, cycling through Tuscany, or going on a safari in Kenya. For years, the small businesses and local experts who run these trips have been stuck using messy spreadsheets, countless emails, and complicated payment methods.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">WeTravel is changing that. We build the tools that empower any entrepreneur to launch and grow their own travel business. Our platform takes care of the business behind the trip: proposals, bookings, payments and customer management. That lets organizers focus on what they do best: designing and leading unforgettable experiences.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What's the role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As organizers grow, WeTravel stops being a standalone tool and becomes part of their stack. A tour operator wants bookings to flow into their own tools, payments to land in their accounting system, and leads to sync with their CRM. Getting that right is often what wins the deal, and what keeps the customer for years.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In practice, you're the technical partner organizers and our commercial team rely on, from the first discovery call to a smooth go-live. You'll understand how a travel business runs, design how WeTravel fits into it, and prove it works using our public APIs, webhooks and no-code tools like Zapier.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">But the role goes beyond individual customers. As more organizers connect WeTravel to their business, every integration teaches us something about what the platform should do next. We want Solution Engineering to be the voice of our customers' integration needs inside engineering, and a stakeholder for WeTravel's public interfaces. You'll spot the patterns across deals, decide what should become a platform capability instead of a one-off, and work with product engineering teams to make it happen. A few areas where we'll need you:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Public API and webhooks:</strong> bring input in the roadmap of our APIs based on what customers actually try to build</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Integration playbooks:</strong> turn recurring setups into reusable guides, templates and reference implementations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pre-sales at scale:</strong> create demos, sample and solution blueprints that help our sales team answer technical questions confidently, without needing an engineer on every call</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our success here will make WeTravel easy to adopt for larger and more complex organizers, and will let our team support many more customers without growing linearly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you'll do day-to-day</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your time will be split roughly evenly between helping us win deals and helping customers succeed after they sign.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pre-sales</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join Account Executives on discovery and demo calls, uncover the prospect's technical requirements, and map their workflows to WeTravel</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scope integrations and migrations, answer security and technical questionnaires, and give honest answers on what's possible today and what isn't</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build tailored demos and quick proofs of concept that show how WeTravel plugs into the prospect's existing tools</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Implementation and support</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guide customers and their developers through integrations with Google Analytics, Zapier, QuickBooks, our public APIs and webhooks, as well as data migrations, complex inventory setups and go-live</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Troubleshoot complex integration issues with customers, and make sure what you learn flows back into our docs, playbooks and product</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write scripts, prototypes and sample apps (Python, JavaScript, Postman collections, Zapier flows) that unblock customers and can be reused by others</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shaping the platform</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent customer integration needs in product and engineering planning, backed by data from deals and tickets</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain our integration documentation, playbooks and internal knowledge base</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use AI tools to automate the repetitive parts of the job, from ticket triage to generating integration code</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>What success looks like</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First month:</strong> you know our product, APIs and the most common integration setups. You've shadowed sales calls and resolved your first technical tickets end-to-end.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First three months:</strong> you run technical discovery and demos on your own, own customer implementations through go-live, and have shipped reusable assets .</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First six months:</strong> you own a clear picture of what our customers try to build with WeTravel, and bring data-backed proposals into engineering planning. Your playbooks and tools mean the team takes on more customers with less custom work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>How we work</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll be part of the Solutions Engineering team within our Engineering organisation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll work closely with Sales, Onboarding, Account Management, Product and Engineering, and have a seat at the table in deal reviews.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're focused on impact. We move quickly, value clarity, and adapt our processes based on what works.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We'd rather build something once and automated than solve it ten times by hand.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We use the latest hardware and are constantly on the lookout for better tools and ways to work, including AI assistants and agents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our tools: REST APIs, Postman, Zapier, HubSpot, Snowflake. Our platform runs on React/TypeScript, Ruby on Rails, Python and Go microservices on Kubernetes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>You should apply if you have</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Basic qualifications</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of 7+ years in a customer-facing technical role (Solutions Engineer, Sales Engineer, Technical Account Manager, Integration Engineer or similar)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on fluency with REST APIs, webhooks, JSON and authentication (API keys, OAuth). You can read API docs, debug a failing request and explain why it failed</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with integration tools like Zapier: you can design, troubleshoot and optimise automated workflows</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort writing scripts and prototypes in at least one language (JavaScript/TypeScript, Python, Ruby or Go)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading technical discovery and demos with prospects, and owning implementations through go-live</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to explain complex technical topics to non-technical people, and to translate customer needs into clear requirements for engineers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good judgment about when to solve a problem for one customer and when to push for a platform solution</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication skills in English and experience working in multicultural, distributed teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience using AI assistants like Claude, Cursor or ChatGPT to speed up your work</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Preferred qualifications</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in travel, tourism or booking platforms, including inventory and availability setups</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of payments, accounting, analytics or CRM integrations (e.g. QuickBooks, Xero, Google Analytics, HubSpot, Salesforce)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience influencing API design or a developer platform roadmap</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Don’t tick every box? If the role excites you and you’ve got most of what we’re looking for, we’d still love to hear from you</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>Why join us?</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make a real impact:</strong> you'll help build the operating system for the multi-day group travel industry, empowering thousands of organizers and millions of travelers worldwide.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shape the platform, not just tickets:</strong> your insights from customers will directly impact what our engineering teams build.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work at the intersection of tech and business:</strong> you'll partner with Sales, Customer Success and Engineering every week, and see the direct impact of your work on deals won and customers launched.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Help build the team:</strong> you'll join a small team at an inflection point, with real ownership over how Solutions Engineering works at WeTravel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><br />Benefits</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous "Time to Recharge" policy - enjoy unlimited paid time off to rest, recharge, and show up as your best self.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work remotely for a maximum of 4 weeks per calendar year.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2-week cross-functional onboarding program.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cycle-to-work scheme (Swapfiets subscription) or commuting reimbursement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monday and Thursday lunches and after-work social events.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Beautiful office in central Amsterdam – rooftop garden and right by Rokin metro.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Extensive paid family leave.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Three paid volunteer days per year - take time to give back to causes you care about, on us.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cutting-edge equipment and tools to set you up for success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employer-sponsored pension plan with a 2% employer contribution deposited into your individual pension account<em>.</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to a 10% group discount on supplementary/additional health insurance (aanvullende verzekeringen), with the same discount available to eligible family members.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to our Booking Marketplace: Book hotels and flights for personal travel at exclusive discounted rates.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join an international, travel-loving team with a passion for adventure and innovation</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ready to build something meaningful? Apply now.</p><h2></h2><h2>Equal Opportunities</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">WeTravel is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. If you're excited about this opportunity and believe you're a good fit, we encourage you to apply and join us in transforming the travel industry!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/wetravel/senior-solutions-engineer-amsterdam-487719","tags":["Engineering & Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794336038},{"slug":"manager-service-operations-ai-amstelveen-68836","company_name":"Staffplanning B.V.","title":"Manager Service Operations & AI","description":"<p>Ben jij een ervaren IT Operations Manager die niet alleen een supportorganisatie kan aansturen, maar ook kansen ziet om dienstverlening slimmer en efficiënter te maken met AI? Dan hebben wij een interessante uitdaging voor je.</p><p>Voor Fivespark, een ambitieuze Managed Service Provider in Amstelveen, zoeken wij een Manager Service Operations & AI. In deze veelzijdige functie combineer je operationeel leiderschap met procesverbetering, automatisering en de verdere ontwikkeling van een eigen AI-agent.</p><p>Je krijgt de verantwoordelijkheid over een team van 12 supportprofessionals én speelt een belangrijke rol in de transformatie naar een steeds verder geautomatiseerde IT-dienstverlening.</p><h2>Over Fivespark</h2><p>Fivespark is een innovatieve Managed Service Provider die bedrijven en overheden ondersteunt met moderne IT-oplossingen.</p><p>De organisatie werkt aan de Managed Service Provider van de toekomst, waarin automatisering, kunstmatige intelligentie en datagedreven processen een steeds grotere rol spelen.</p><p>Een belangrijk onderdeel hiervan is Sparkle, een intern ontwikkelde AI-agent die nu al ondersteunt bij ticketregistratie, triage, klantvragen en routering. De ambitie is om Sparkle verder te ontwikkelen tot een volwaardige digitale collega die steeds meer operationele processen zelfstandig en betrouwbaar kan uitvoeren.</p><p>De organisatie kenmerkt zich door korte lijnen, een informele werksfeer en veel ruimte voor eigen initiatief en verantwoordelijkheid.</p><h2>Wat ga je doen?</h2><p>Als Manager Service Operations & AI ben je verantwoordelijk voor de dagelijkse aansturing en verdere professionalisering van de tweedelijns supportorganisatie. Tegelijkertijd speel je een centrale rol in het ontwikkelen en implementeren van AI en automatisering.</p><p>Je werkzaamheden bestaan uit vier belangrijke onderdelen.</p><h3>Leidinggeven aan de supportorganisatie</h3><ul><li><p>Je geeft leiding aan een team van 12 tweedelijns supportmedewerkers.</p></li><li><p>Je coacht en ontwikkelt medewerkers en zorgt voor duidelijke prioriteiten, structuur en samenwerking.</p></li><li><p>Je bewaakt de kwaliteit, capaciteit, continuïteit en prestaties van de dienstverlening.</p></li><li><p>Je signaleert knelpunten en vertaalt deze naar concrete verbeteracties.</p></li></ul><h3>Doorontwikkelen van AI-agent Sparkle</h3><ul><li><p>Je bent functioneel eigenaar van Sparkle en bepaalt mede de visie, roadmap en prioriteiten.</p></li><li><p>Je vertaalt operationele uitdagingen naar praktische AI-toepassingen.</p></li><li><p>Je zorgt ervoor dat Sparkle veilig, betrouwbaar en gebruiksvriendelijk functioneert.</p></li><li><p>Je werkt samen met technische specialisten aan de verdere ontwikkeling van deze digitale collega.</p></li></ul><h3>Processen verbeteren en automatiseren</h3><ul><li><p>Je analyseert bestaande operationele processen en identificeert mogelijkheden voor automatisering.</p></li><li><p>Je optimaliseert workflows, kennisbanken en werkinstructies.</p></li><li><p>Je zorgt voor een goede samenwerking tussen medewerkers en AI.</p></li><li><p>Je draagt bij aan de ambitie om minimaal 75% van de standaard operationele processen met AI te ondersteunen of volledig te automatiseren.</p></li></ul><h3>Verandering begeleiden</h3><ul><li><p>Je werkt samen met Operations, Software Development, Business Consultancy en externe partners.</p></li><li><p>Je begeleidt medewerkers in de overgang naar een meer AI-gedreven manier van werken.</p></li><li><p>Je creëert draagvlak, communiceert helder en zorgt ervoor dat veranderingen daadwerkelijk worden doorgevoerd.</p></li></ul><h2>Wie zoeken wij?</h2><p>Wij zoeken een operationeel sterke manager die structuur weet aan te brengen, medewerkers kan motiveren en tegelijkertijd vooruitkijkt naar de mogelijkheden van nieuwe technologie.</p><p>Je begrijpt hoe een IT-supportorganisatie werkt, weet hoe je processen beheersbaar en voorspelbaar maakt en krijgt energie van het continu verbeteren van de dienstverlening.</p><p>Daarnaast beschik je over:</p><ul><li><p>Hbo- of wo-werk- en -denkniveau.</p></li><li><p>Minimaal 5 jaar ervaring binnen Managed Services, ICT Operations of IT Service Management.</p></li><li><p>Ervaring met het aansturing, coachen en ontwikkelen van operationele teams.</p></li><li><p>Goede kennis van ITIL-processen en servicemanagement.</p></li><li><p>Affiniteit met AI, automatisering en digitale innovatie.</p></li><li><p>Sterke analytische en organisatorische vaardigheden.</p></li><li><p>Het vermogen om technische mogelijkheden te vertalen naar concrete operationele verbeteringen.</p></li><li><p>Goede communicatieve vaardigheden en ervaring met verandermanagement.</p></li></ul><p>Je hoeft geen AI-developer te zijn. We zoeken juist iemand die begrijpt hoe je AI en automatisering succesvol inzet binnen een operationele IT-organisatie en medewerkers hierin weet mee te nemen.</p><h2>Wat kun je verwachten?</h2><p>Je komt rechtstreeks in dienst bij onze opdrachtgever en krijgt een sleutelrol binnen een organisatie die volop investeert in de toekomst van IT-dienstverlening.</p><p>Je kunt rekenen op:</p><ul><li><p>Een bruto maandsalaris van €4.487 tot €6.494, afhankelijk van kennis en ervaring.</p></li><li><p>Een mobiliteitsbudget van €850 per maand, vrij in te zetten op de manier die bij jou past.</p></li><li><p>Een fulltime dienstverband.</p></li><li><p>Flexibele werkmogelijkheden en ruimte om hybride te werken.</p></li><li><p>Veel zelfstandigheid en directe invloed op de ontwikkeling van de organisatie.</p></li><li><p>Ruime mogelijkheden voor persoonlijke en professionele ontwikkeling.</p></li><li><p>De kans om actief bij te dragen aan innovatieve AI- en automatiseringsprojecten.</p></li><li><p>Een informele en professionele werkomgeving met korte lijnen.</p></li><li><p>Een betrokken team van collega's dat samenwerkt aan verbetering en innovatie.</p></li></ul><h2>Waarom is dit een interessante functie?</h2><p>Wat deze rol bijzonder maakt, is de combinatie van peoplemanagement, operationele verantwoordelijkheid en AI-innovatie.</p><p>Je krijgt niet alleen de opdracht om een bestaande supportorganisatie goed te laten functioneren, maar ook om deze klaar te maken voor de toekomst.</p><p>Daarbij krijg je de ruimte om processen structureel te verbeteren, nieuwe technologie toe te passen en daadwerkelijk invloed uit te oefenen op de manier waarop IT-dienstverlening wordt georganiseerd.</p><p>Een mooie uitdaging voor een ervaren Service Delivery Manager, IT Operations Manager of Support Manager die toe is aan een volgende stap.</p><h2>Interesse?</h2><p>Wil jij leidinggeven aan een IT-supportorganisatie én een belangrijke rol spelen in de verdere ontwikkeling van AI binnen Managed Services?</p><p>Dan komen wij graag met je in contact!</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/staffplanning-bv/manager-service-operations-ai-amstelveen-68836","tags":["Business Operations"],"job_types":["Vast contract","manager / supervisor"],"location":"Amstelveen","created_at":1794326453},{"slug":"support-engineer-amstelveen-149592","company_name":"Staffplanning B.V.","title":"Support Engineer","description":"<p>Als Support Engineer los je technische vraagstukken van klanten op en zorg je dat IT-beheer en connectiviteit optimaal blijven functioneren. Bij Fivespark krijg je de ruimte om je verder te ontwikkelen, verantwoordelijkheid te nemen en direct impact te maken bij onze klanten.</p><h2>Maak kennis met Fivespark</h2><p>Fivespark adviseert en ondersteunt bedrijven en overheden met strategische ICT‑oplossingen. Onze missie: de creatieve en technische partner zijn voor de ICT‑uitdagingen van onze klanten. Dit doen we met een team van ruim 70 proactieve en enthousiaste medewerkers, waaronder ervaren specialisten.</p><h2>Wat ga je doen?</h2><p>Als Support Engineer ben jij het aanspreekpunt voor onze klanten. Je ondersteunt gebruikers bij uiteenlopende technische vragen en zorgt dat incidenten deskundig en klantgericht worden opgelost. Afhankelijk van jouw achtergrond en ontwikkelwensen, ligt de nadruk in jouw werk op IT-beheer, connectiviteit of een combinatie daarvan.</p><p>Je werkzaamheden bestaan uit:</p><ul><li><p>Je helpt klanten via telefoon en mail en legt meldingen nauwkeurig vast in ons ticketsysteem</p></li><li><p>Je analyseert problemen, stelt de juiste vragen en begeleidt klanten naar een passende oplossing</p></li></ul><p>Voor connectiviteit ligt de focus op:</p><ul><li><p>Je ondersteunt bij het opleveren, configureren en beheren van internet- en telefoniediensten</p></li><li><p>Je geeft advies op locatie en voert VoIP-installaties en updates zorgvuldig uit</p></li><li><p>Je werkt met platforms zoals Broadsoft en apparatuur zoals Draytek/Mikrotik/SonicWall</p></li></ul><p>Voor IT-beheer ligt de focus op:</p><ul><li><p>Je helpt gebruikers bij werkplekvraagstukken, incidenten en de installatie van hardware en software</p></li><li><p>Je draagt zorg voor de installatie, documentatie en het onderhoud van ICT-middelen</p></li></ul><h2>Wat neem je mee?</h2><p>Als Support Engineer bij Fivespark krijg je de ruimte om verschil te maken. Je werkt in een omgeving waar jouw expertise wordt gewaardeerd en waar je kunt groeien. Herken jij jezelf in onderstaande punten? Dan is dit jouw kans:</p><ul><li><p>Je hebt werkervaring in een soortgelijke rol (bij voorkeur 2 tot 4 jaar)</p></li><li><p>Je hebt ervaring met serviceverlening (face-to-face, digitaal en telefonisch)</p></li><li><p>Ervaring met ticketsystemen zoals Freshservice of Topdesk is een pré</p></li><li><p>Je werkt nauwkeurig, documenteert helder en houdt overzicht</p></li><li><p>Je denkt mee met de klant en pakt problemen actief op</p></li><li><p>Je hebt ervaring met ICT, telecom en/of VoIP. Binnen telecom heb je in ieder geval ervaring met Broadsoft, Draytek en Mikrotik. Kennis van SonicWall is een pré</p></li><li><p>Je beheerst de Nederlandse taal vloeiend, zowel mondeling als schriftelijk</p></li></ul><h2>Wat bieden wij?</h2><p>Fivespark biedt een fijne werkomgeving, een plek waar jij als professional kunt groeien. Je krijgt de ruimte om verantwoordelijkheid te nemen, mee te denken en jezelf te ontwikkelen.</p><p>Daarnaast kun je rekenen op de volgende voordelen:</p><ul><li><p>Salaris van €3.010 tot €4.487 bruto per maand</p></li><li><p>Reiskostenvergoeding voor kilometers of OV</p></li><li><p>Vakantiegeld en 25 vakantiedagen</p></li><li><p>Laptop van de zaak</p></li><li><p>Uitzicht op een contract voor onbepaalde tijd</p></li><li><p>Solide pensioenregeling</p></li><li><p>Persoonlijk opleidingsbudget en ruimte voor trainingen</p></li><li><p>Gezellige teamuitjes, huiselijke sfeer en alles wat je nodig hebt</p></li><li><p>Een informeel team waarin iedereen zichzelf kan zijn</p></li></ul><h2>Solliciteer</h2><p>Solliciteer nu en maak deel uit van Fivespark. Wij kijken ernaar uit om je te ontmoeten!</p><p>Heb je vragen over het proces of de vacature? Neem gerust contact op met Staffplanning. Dat kan via mail of telefonisch op 073-7505000</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/staffplanning-bv/support-engineer-amstelveen-149592","tags":["Helpdesk"],"job_types":["Vast contract","professional / ervaren"],"location":"Amstelveen","created_at":1794326453},{"slug":"medior-senior-full-stack-developer-delft-484749","company_name":"Momo Medical","title":"Medior/Senior Full Stack Developer","description":"<p><span style="color:#172E73">Do you want to work in a dynamic environment where your code really makes a difference? Are you a passionate developer who enjoys tackling complex technical challenges?</span></p><p><span style="color:#172E73">Join the Customer Champions team and create a world-class app in which all the value of the Momo platform comes together. Help us create reusable, and above all, user-friendly components and interactions that make caregivers love the app.<br></span></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#D071D0">Who is Momo?</span></strong></h3><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#172E73">Momo Medical is a fast-growing and ambitious scale-up, tackling one of the biggest societal challenges: the future of elderly care. Over the next decade, demand for care is expected to double, while 30% of the current workforce is projected to retire. Our innovative solutions aim to reduce the pressure on healthcare workers while improving the quality of care for residents.<br></span></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#D071D0">The most valuable aspects of the role</span></strong></h3><p><span style="color:#172E73">🚀 Your work </span><strong><span style="color:#172E73">defines</span></strong><span style="color:#172E73"> the way caregivers interact with the app as well as how it </span><strong><span style="color:#172E73">looks</span></strong><span style="color:#172E73">. All while staying in very close contact with them to understand exactly what they need.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="color:#172E73">⚓ </span><strong><span style="color:#172E73">Work together with many teams</span></strong><span style="color:#172E73">, such as production, customer success, and hardware, to translate real-world problems into reliable software.</span></p><p><span style="color:#172E73">💛 You contribute to </span><strong><span style="color:#172E73">better care for nursing home residents</span></strong><span style="color:#172E73"> and help </span><strong><span style="color:#172E73">reduce the workload for healthcare professionals</span></strong><span style="color:#172E73">.</span></p><p><span style="color:#172E73">&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#101726">📍</span><span style="color:#172E73"> You’re available </span><strong><span style="color:#172E73">32 - 40 hours per week</span></strong><span style="color:#172E73"> and happy to spend at least 4 days per week with the team in Delft.</span></p><p><span style="color:#172E73">&nbsp;🎊 Thursday pizza nights, Friday drinks, team activities, travel allowance, pension plan, and plenty of growth opportunities that match your ambitions.<br></span></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#D071D0">Your key responsibilities</span></strong></h3><p><span style="color:#172E73">As part of a multidisciplinary team you will work on innovative solutions that have a direct impact on healthcare professionals in the Netherlands and abroad. You will have the opportunity to develop your skills, specialize or grow into a team leader role. You can work on the front-end or the back-end, or even better: both!<br></span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#172E73">Your key responsibilities include:</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#172E73">Maintain and improve the connection between business logic and UI in our </span><strong><span style="color:#172E73">Flutter</span></strong><span style="color:#172E73"> app by employing Bloc and Clean Architecture.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#172E73">Design, build, and maintain </span><strong><span style="color:#172E73">TypeScript services </span></strong><span style="color:#172E73">that drive the app to thousands of phones simultaneously. .</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#172E73">Design </span><strong><span style="color:#172E73">event-driven systems</span></strong><span style="color:#172E73"> that provide the app with the freshest data possible</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#172E73">Automate manual workflows</span></strong><span style="color:#172E73"> and improve reliability through observability, testing, and CI/CD.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#172E73">Mentor teammates, set technical direction, and help prioritize the roadmap.<br></span></p></li></ul><h3><strong><span style="color:#D071D0">Who are you?</span></strong></h3><ul><li><p><span style="color:#172E73">You have an advanced skill set of </span><strong><span style="color:#172E73">Flutter, Node,</span></strong><span style="color:#172E73"> </span><strong><span style="color:#172E73">and TypeScript</span></strong><span style="color:#172E73">,</span><strong><span style="color:#172E73"> </span></strong><span style="color:#172E73">backed by a track record of delivering full-stack features end-to-end in fast-paced environments.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#172E73">You validate your features with </span><strong><span style="color:#172E73">automated tests</span></strong><span style="color:#172E73">, ranging from unit-tests to fully automated widget tests and end-to-end tests.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#172E73">You’re comfortable </span><strong><span style="color:#172E73">modelling data and tuning performance</span></strong><span style="color:#172E73"> in relational databases such as PostgreSQL.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#172E73">A </span><strong><span style="color:#172E73">good level of English</span></strong><span style="color:#172E73"> is required, and it is a plus if you can speak Dutch.&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#172E73">You enjoy collaborating with colleagues across the company and keeping multiple initiatives moving forward.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#101726">Y</span><span style="color:#172E73">ou’re available </span><strong><span style="color:#172E73">32–40 hours per week</span></strong><span style="color:#172E73"> and happy to spend at least four days a week with the team in Delft.<br></span></p></li></ul><h3><strong><span style="color:#D071D0">Why join Momo Medical?</span></strong></h3><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#172E73">Because you want to make a difference in healthcare at home and abroad. Because you are excited about a fast-growing scale-up where no two days are the same. And because you want to work with young, enthusiastic and talented international colleagues who all work hard to make healthcare a little bit better every day.</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#172E73">Salary: €4,000–5,000 (medior) or €5,000–6,000 (senior) per month based on 40 hours, plus 8% holiday allowance.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#172E73">30 vacation days per year to pick your own holidays (celebrate Christmas, Eid Al-Fitr, or any other holiday of your choice!).</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#172E73">Hybrid working, and a laptop of your choice.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#172E73">Pension plan and travel reimbursement</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#172E73">Guided mentorship and clear paths toward tech lead or specialist roles.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#172E73">Provided lunches, weekly company drinks and dinners, and regular team and company events.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#172E73">Reimbursement of travel expenses and a pension plan<br></span></p></li></ul><h3><strong><span style="color:#D071D0">Good to know</span></strong></h3><p><strong><span style="color:#172E73">Tech at Momo</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#172E73">At Momo, we use the following tools: Flutter, Swift, Kotlin, JavaScript, React, TypeScript, Express, Vitest, Node, PostgreSQL, Docker, Testcontainers, GitHub, and AWS.</span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#172E73">What are the next steps?</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#172E73">First, we’ll review your CV and motivation to get a sense of how you are and to envision how you might fit within our team. After that, you’ll receive a short take-home assignment that helps us understand how you think, and you get insights into the kind of work we do at Momo. The next step is a chat at our offices in Delft, where we can go more in-depth on the role, the team and the Momo culture. Then, as a final exploration, you’ll have the chance to spend a work-along day with us to experience a day at Momo and to meet more people working on the same mission. When both you and we see the match, we’ll share an offer and start the onboarding process so you can join us in supporting caregivers!</span></p> <br> <p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/momo-medical/medior-senior-full-stack-developer-delft-484749","tags":["Development - Customer Champions"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Delft, Zuid-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1794324681},{"slug":"senior-china-research-analyst-eindhoven-3607","company_name":"Datenna BV","title":"Senior China Research Analyst","description":"<p><span style="color:#000000">Datenna is a fast-growing tech scale-up combining cutting-edge OSINT and AI technologies to provide governments with critical insights into China's techno-economic landscape. Our platform transforms open-source intelligence into actionable insights through advanced data processing and analysis.</span></p><p><span style="color:#000000"><br></span><strong><span style="color:#000000">The Role: <br></span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Do you enjoy turning complex data into strategic insights that drive critical decisions? As a Senior China Research Analyst, you will lead analytical research projects for our government clients. You'll turn their most pressing questions about China's technology, industrial, and defence-industrial landscape into data-driven reports and the datasets behind them. You'll work with Datenna's data on patents, procurement, research funding, and companies, and go beyond it when a question demands, to find the patterns and connections that inform high-stakes policy and security decisions.</span><span style="color:#4A4A4A">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW266190147 BCX4"><span style="color:#4A4A4A"><br></span><span style="color:#121317">You'll independently manage several client research projects at a time, from scoping through final delivery, using both qualitative and quantitative analysis across China's corporate, academic, defence, and technology sectors. Client questions often start ambiguous and open-ended, and topics range widely, from advanced materials to semiconductors and aerospace. You'll work through uncertainty, get up to speed quickly on unfamiliar technologies, design creative analytical approaches when the path isn't obvious, and refine your research direction as new information emerges. The role needs strong China expertise, Chinese-language research skills, the ability to work autonomously, and clear communication with senior government stakeholders.</span><span style="color:#4A4A4A">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="color:#000000">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Your mission at Datenna:</span></strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234141466 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234141466 BCX4"><strong><span style="color:#1B2A39">Lead end-to-end research delivery: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Take full ownership of research projects, from initial scoping and analysis through to final deliverables.</span><span style="color:#4A4A4A">&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234141466 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234141466 BCX4"><strong><span style="color:#1B2A39">Design the research: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Turn open-ended client questions into sound research design, and build new analytical frameworks when standard methods don't fit.</span><span style="color:#4A4A4A">&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234141466 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234141466 BCX4"><strong><span style="color:#1B2A39">Build and analyse the evidence base: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Work directly with Chinese-language sources and Datenna's data on entities, patents, procurement, and research funding to map the actors, links, and trends that answer the client's question.</span><span style="color:#4A4A4A">&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234141466 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234141466 BCX4"><strong><span style="color:#1B2A39">Set the quality bar: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Review colleagues' deliverables independently, verify findings against the underlying data, and guide Analysts on their research approach.</span><span style="color:#4A4A4A">&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234141466 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234141466 BCX4"><strong><span style="color:#1B2A39">Work with AI, with judgement: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Use AI-assisted research tools to work faster and at greater scale. You own the interpretation and verify every output.</span><span style="color:#4A4A4A">&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234141466 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234141466 BCX4"><strong><span style="color:#1B2A39">Contribute to the China Research Lab: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">The Lab is our exploratory research track. It develops the methods, tools, and data sources that shape where China research at Datenna is heading, and tests them through internal R&amp;D. You will dedicate part of your time to Lab initiatives, such as prototyping a new analytical approach, scouting and testing new sources, or contributing to webinars and publications.</span><span style="color:#4A4A4A">&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234141466 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234141466 BCX4"><strong><span style="color:#1B2A39">Strengthen the data and product: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Turn what you learn on client projects into data and product improvements, working with the Product and Data teams.</span><span style="color:#4A4A4A">&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#000000"><br>What makes you a great candidate:</span><span style="color:#1B2A39"><br>Core requirements</span></strong><span style="color:#1B2A39">&nbsp;</span></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW128869584 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW128869584 BCX4"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Experience: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">5–8 years of professional experience in China-focused research, analysis, or related fields.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW128869584 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW128869584 BCX4"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Deep China expertise: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Strong knowledge of Chinese industry, economy, policy, the defence-industrial base, and the technology and research landscape.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW128869584 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW128869584 BCX4"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Analytical excellence: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Exceptional pattern recognition and analytical skills to connect the dots between corporate, state, and military actors in China's techno-economic landscape.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW128869584 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW128869584 BCX4"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Comfort with ambiguity: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Proven ability to tackle research questions where the analytical path isn't predetermined, designing creative approaches and adapting as you learn.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW128869584 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW128869584 BCX4"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Chinese language proficiency: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Professional reading proficiency in Chinese (minimum HSK5, HSK6 preferred) to work directly with Chinese-language sources such as technical literature, patents, procurement notices, and policy documents, and to build and verify Chinese technical terminology for data retrieval.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW128869584 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW128869584 BCX4"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Self-directed project management: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Proven ability to independently break down complex research questions, run several multi-week projects in parallel against fixed client deadlines, and deliver high-quality output with minimal oversight.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW128869584 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW128869584 BCX4"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Quality ownership: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">An evidence-first approach. You trace every claim back to its source records, catch inconsistencies in data and drafts, and review others' work independently and constructively.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW105742209 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW105742209 BCX4"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Communication skills: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Strong written and verbal communication, including precise, concise English writing for an international readership. You are comfortable presenting complex analysis to senior government stakeholders and refining requirements through client dialogue.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW105742209 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW105742209 BCX4"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Methodological versatility: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Proficiency in both qualitative and quantitative research methods.</span><span style="color:#4A4A4A">&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW147289894 BCX4"><strong><span style="color:#1B2A39"><br>Technical skills</span></strong><span style="color:#1B2A39">&nbsp;</span></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW147289894 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW147289894 BCX4"><span style="color:#121317">Working proficiency in SQL and/or Python to query, clean, and structure large datasets, plus advanced Excel.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW147289894 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW147289894 BCX4"><span style="color:#121317">Hands-on experience using LLM-based tools in research, with a clear sense of where their output needs human verification.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW147289894 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW147289894 BCX4"><span style="color:#121317">Familiarity with data-quality work such as deduplication and entity resolution.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW147289894 BCX4"><strong><span style="color:#121317"><br>Nice to have</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">&nbsp;</span></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW147289894 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW147289894 BCX4"><span style="color:#121317">Experience in the technology, science, and research sector within governmental organisations, think tanks, or international corporate settings.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW147289894 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW147289894 BCX4"><span style="color:#121317">Background conducting research for external clients or stakeholders.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW147289894 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW147289894 BCX4"><span style="color:#121317">Experience analysing patents, public procurement, research funding, or corporate registry data.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW147289894 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW147289894 BCX4"><span style="color:#121317">Experience collecting web data from Chinese-language sources, or with BI tools such as Metabase.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW147289894 BCX4"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW147289894 BCX4"><span style="color:#121317">A technical or scientific background (for example materials science, engineering, or physics) relevant to dual-use technology topics.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><em><span style="color:#000000">*Please know that applicants may be subject to a screening process.*</span></em></strong></p> <br> <ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Work on globally impactful projects in geopolitical intelligence</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Lead innovation in OSINT and AI technologies</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Competitive compensation and benefits</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Dynamic, international team environment</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Significant growth opportunities in a scale-up</span></p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;"><em><span style="color:#121317">When you apply to this position, we will process your personal data according to our </span><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://datenna.com/recruitment-privacy-notice.pdf"><span style="color:#121317">Recruitment Privacy Notice</span></a></u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://datenna.com/recruitment-privacy-notice.pdf"><span style="color:#121317">.</span></a></em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/datenna-bv/senior-china-research-analyst-eindhoven-3607","tags":["Research"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Eindhoven, Noord-Brabant, Netherlands","created_at":1794324679},{"slug":"senior-director-head-of-quality-responsible-person-international-265713","company_name":"Bridgebio","title":"Senior Director, Head of Quality & Responsible Person, International ","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Mavericks Wanted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;When was the last time you achieved the impossible? If that thought feels overwhelming, you might want to pause here, but if it sparks excitement...read on&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;In 2015, we pioneered a “moneyball for biotech” approach, pooling projects and promising early-stage research from academia together under one financial umbrella to reduce risk and unleash innovation. This model allows science and small teams of experts to lead the way. We build bridges to groundbreaking advancements in rare&amp;nbsp;disease, and&amp;nbsp;develop life-changing medicines for patients with unmet needs as fast as humanly possible. &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Together we define white space, push boundaries, and empower people to solve problems. If you&#39;re someone who defies convention, join us and work alongside some of the most respected minds in the industry. Together, we&#39;ll&amp;nbsp;ask&amp;nbsp;&quot;why not?&quot; and help reengineer the future of biopharma. At BridgeBio, we value curiosity and experimentation—including the ethical &amp;amp; thoughtful use of AI to improve clarity, speed, and quality of work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Sr Director, Head of Quality &amp;amp; Responsible Person, International, leads quality for infigratinib, and will be the designated Responsible Person on the entity&#39;s wholesale distribution authorisation. The role reports to the Head of Quality, QED, with a dotted line to local managing director, and is based in the Netherlands. If the entity becomes the marketing authorisation holder for infigratinib, the role also covers the related MAH quality duties. The role holds an unrestricted right of escalation to the entity&#39;s full board and is independent of commercial operations and of manufacturing/supply with EU-GDP guidelines, relevant EU directives (including the Falsified Medicines Directive), Dutch Medicines Act, and public service requirements. This role acts as a QA liaison of BridgeBio&#39;s contract service providers (CSPs), providing oversight of lot release activities. This role includes reviewing and approving batch records, certificates of analysis, and compliance documents, providing quality review of deviations, change controls, and CAPAs related to assigned CSPs, collaborating closely with CSPs and internal teams such as quality control, manufacturing, regulatory affairs, and supply chain. The role builds and leads a small quality team (deputy RP, QA compliance/QMS, QA operations/GDP), owns the quality management system across the Skeletal Dysplasia assets, and leads WDA licensing, inspection readiness and potentially subsequent MIA readiness, if needed in the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Major Responsibilities / Accountabilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the named Responsible Person on the WDA: release for distribution, recall decisions, and GDP compliance of the entity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leads and develops the entity&#39;s quality team: deputy RP, QA compliance/QMS, and QA operations/GDP; and QP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manages and improves the Quality Management System (QMS) across the entity&#39;s assets in alignment with the established QMS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the WDA application and IGJ inspection readiness; prepare subsequent MIA readiness (QP recruitment, import and batch-certification processes)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the quality agreement matrix: includes Quality oversight of contract service providers, 3PLs, distributors and intercompany interfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a Quality liaison and provide oversight and quality support of assigned contract service providers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform quality review of assigned quality events such as deviations, change controls, supplier notifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review master manufacturing batch records, including related documents such as specifications, analytical and microbiological methods, stability study protocols, and label proofs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage lot release activities and communication of lot release schedules to key stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate manufacturing deficiencies/non-conformances to management and work with CSPs to ensure timely resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review process and method validation protocols and reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review analytical test results to ensure compliance with approved specifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in updating CMC sections of regulatory and quality documents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in internal and external project team meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Other QA/Responsible Person related responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure accuracy of quality of records per GDP requirements including GDPs are implemented and maintained in the quality management system requirements for WDA license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and coordinate return, rejected, falsified products, recall operations of medicinal products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide oversight of GDP and GMP activities of active pharmaceutical ingredients (API)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure WDA and API registration is current with commercial supply chain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate and leads EU/ROW regulatory inspections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate and oversee GMP vendor qualification program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the EU/ROW internal audit program, internal training program and ensure data integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and review governing procedures as needed (e.g., SOPs, WIs, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Where You’ll Work&amp;nbsp; &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a Netherlands based remote role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel 30% of time is expected&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Who you are&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS/MS degree preferably in operations, science, pharmacy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A diploma, certificate, or other evidence of formal qualifications on completion of GDP/GDP-API training required for registration as an RP by the competent authorities in the Netherlands&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in pharmaceutical quality, including significant GDP / distribution quality experience; prior appointment as (or eligibility to be) a Responsible Person strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading regulatory inspections with EU competent authorities (IGJ preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience of managing third party vendors (CMOs, CTLs, 3PLs, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior relevant knowledge and experience related to the distribution of medical products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of supply chain concepts, supplier management, inventory management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive knowledge of US/EU GMPs /GDPs and associated guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working in a highly regulated environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven leadership of quality teams; experience building quality functions or systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding the EU and particularly IGJ regulations in relation to the wholesale distribution of medicines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong planning and time management skills with ability to prioritize workload&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills, with keen attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in document and presentation office tools (Microsoft Office, Google Docs, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic understanding of data concepts and enterprise resource planning (ERP) systems e.g., SAP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ready to embrace company core values and diverse corporate culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Rewarding Those Who Make the Mission Possible&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have high expectations for our team members. We make sure those working hard for patients are rewarded and cared for in return.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market leading compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid work model - we value your flexibility in how you work, but encourage time in the office to strengthen our culture, collaboration, and sense of community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We provide career development through regular feedback, continuous education and professional development programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We celebrate strong performance with financial rewards, peer-to-peer recognition, and growth opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a global company, our comprehensive benefits may vary based on location.&amp;nbsp; &lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We have high expectations for our team members. We make sure those working hard for patients are rewarded and cared for in return.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
