&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Master the End-to-End Creative Process:&lt;/strong&gt; Pitch bold ideas, direct colleagues on camera, shoot mobile-first, and cut the final edit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Turn Raw Stories into High-Engagement Assets:&lt;/strong&gt; Capture real, behind-the-scenes moments and turn everyday footage into clips that our target persona actually wants to watch on LinkedIn and Instagram.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Refine Visual Craft &amp;amp; Brand Consistency:&lt;/strong&gt; Sharpen your eye for pacing, color, and smart branding to make every piece of content look pro and cohesive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Your superpowers&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Currently enrolled student:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently pursuing a Bachelor’s or Master’s in Media, Film, Communication, Design, or a related creative field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong short-form editing chops:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience with Adobe Suite and CapCut, with a strong feel for hooks, retention editing, tempo, sound design, and color grading/color theory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfortable behind the lens:&lt;/strong&gt; Confident shooting content on both a smartphone and a camera, with a solid eye for framing, lighting, and composition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems thinker:&lt;/strong&gt; You know how to build organized project files that can be easily adapted and reused across different social platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Language &amp;amp; Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Fluent in English (Dutch, French, or German is a plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Bonus: Working knowledge of After Effects for animations/graphics, or photography skills.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Don’t tick all the boxes yet? Picnic is the perfect learning environment for the highly ambitious and the deeply curious. If you align with Picnic’s mission, please feel free to send your application through.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Picnic Perks&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;perks-content&quot;&gt;🚀&lt;strong&gt;Every expert was once a beginner!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You’ll have plenty of chances to grow, whether it&#39;s through our casual Lunch &amp;amp; Learn sessions or team specific trainings. We&#39;re especially keen on keeping great talent around; perform well as a working student, and we would love to explore transitioning you into a full-time role.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;perks-content&quot;&gt;🌍&lt;strong&gt;Make a difference&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You’ll work in an awesome startup environment with the freedom to drive your own projects and create a visible impact. Our fully electric vehicles and sustainable business model mean you’ll also be contributing to making the world a better place!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;perks-content&quot;&gt;🤝&lt;strong&gt;Teamwork makes the dream work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;With more than 80 nationalities across 3 countries, you’ll be part of a diverse company with plenty of cool stuff to get involved with, from board game evenings to after-work drinks to our company ski trip and more!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;perks-content&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🥗Fresh Lunch, coffee, and snacks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;perks-content&quot;&gt;Our offices are equipped with fully-fledged coffee bars and a kitchen and chefs. They prepare delicious fresh and warm lunches every day so you can keep your energy up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;perks-content&quot;&gt;💪&lt;strong&gt;Stay healthy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Mental health is important. As well as having the option to speak with Picnic colleagues who act as confidential advisors, our collaboration with OpenUp gives you easy access to professional psychologists, along with workshops and materials.&lt;br&gt;There are plenty of sports communities and events to get involved with, from tennis to yoga to climbing!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;perks-content&quot;&gt;💰&lt;strong&gt;Attractive package&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll receive a gross hourly wage of €16,75 (incl. holiday pay) along with a laptop to support your work. Travel costs can also be reimbursed, depending on your location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/teampicnic/working-student-content-creator-amsterdam-325859","tags":["Students"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794293719},{"slug":"internship-uav-robotics-mechatronics-drone-prototyping-integration-field-testing-delft-234540","company_name":"Fiducial","title":"Internship - UAV Robotics/Mechatronics (Drone Prototyping, Integration & Field Testing)","description":"<h2><strong>Opening</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">WE CANNOT PROVIDE VISA SPONSORSHIP</p><h2><br /><strong>Details</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Preferred starting date: ASAP</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Weekly availability: full-time (5 days/week)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Period: 6 months</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Location: Aerospace Innovation Hub, Delft, the Netherlands</p><h2><br /><strong>About the company</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fiducial is a young but fast-growing deep-tech start-up with big ambitions at the frontier of autonomy, perception, and defence. Currently, we are developing software for advanced on-board UAV situational awareness in military applications. Using low-cost and widely available sensors and compute, our solutions are built for scalability. From there, we plan to develop a line-up of interconnected solutions to safeguard European safety.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our team consists of engineers that are passionate about the technology and solutions they develop. The only time most of us are not thinking about the technology is when we are asleep, and sometimes even then. Our team members have a background in different fields such as Aerospace Engineering, Computational Science and Engineering, Robotics and Computer Graphics. Our office is located in the Aerospace Innovation Hub, a start-up hub located on the TU Delft campus in the faculty of Aerospace Engineering.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work closely with top-tier partners, ranging from government agencies and prime contractors to academic research institutes and other start-ups. Our projects span from large tender orders in collaboration with partners to low TRL research with government agencies. Whether through formal R&amp;D programs or rapid prototyping tracks, we operate at the intersection of innovation and deployment.</p><h3><br /><strong>Your role</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’ve ever spent a weekend building a drone, tuning a flight controller, soldering a power harness, or figuring out why your FPV setup won’t arm, this internship is literally designed for you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a <em>hands-on builder</em> who loves working with real hardware:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">wiring sensors</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">mounting compute boards</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">setting up flight controllers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">testing drones outdoors</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">fixing whatever breaks and making it better</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">If phrases like <em>ArduPilot, PX4, Jetson, ESCs, power distribution, 3D printing, or FPV gear</em> make you smile, you’re the kind of person we want.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not a “sit behind a desk” internship. You will be on the drones. You will be in the field. You will fly.</p><h3><br /><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and integrate hardware onto real drone platforms used in active R&amp;D.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work hands-on with flight controllers (ArduPilot) and compute boards (Jetson, Orange Pi).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deploy and debug embedded perception software.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solder, assemble, and prototype wiring, adapters, mounts, and housings.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3D-print parts and quickly turn ideas into working physical prototypes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support and participate in drone flight tests (you’ll fly regularly).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Troubleshoot issues, iterate fast, and improve our hardware setups.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll see your work fly,  literally!</p><h3><br /><strong>Who you are</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ve built or flown drones / RC systems (any level counts).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You tinker with electronics, FPV, embedded software, or robotics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You enjoy making physical things work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You like fast iteration and getting your hands dirty.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Linux doesn’t scare you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are independent, curious, and resourceful.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We don’t care about grades, we care about what you’ve made.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please include photos/links of:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">your drone builds</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">FPV rigs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">electronics projects</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CAD/3D-printed parts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">GitHub repos</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">anything that shows you build things</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’ve ever crashed something, fixed it, and sent it back into the sky — you’ll fit right in.</p><h3><br /><strong>Requirements</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enrolled in a relevant study (Aerospace, Robotics, Electrical, Mechatronics, Engineering etc.).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Linux basics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interest in UAVs, robotics, embedded systems, or autonomy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">English proficiency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Organized and proactive.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bonus:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">driver’s license, drone pilot license, CAD, 3D printing, soldering, or flight experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">1000 euro monthly compensation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">10 vacation days during internship period.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">(Really) flexible working hours and option to work from home 2 days per week.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have a direct and significant influence on highly innovative products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The opportunity to iterate quickly with tight feedback loops, close to the product. We are innovating, learning is to be expected.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Responsibility over the things you implement, you are the expert on what you build.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The application procedure</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">If after reading the above you are convinced you are the right person for the job, send us some information about yourself; this can be a resume, website or other source, as long as we get a clear impression of your background and skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’ll get back to you ASAP. If we feel you could be a fit for the position, we’ll invite you for an informal introduction so we can get to know you, and equally important, you can get to know us. After this, a technical focused interview could follow.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">If at this point we feel you are the person we are looking for, we’ll discuss the specifics (starting date and period).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Welcome to the team!</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/fiducial/internship-uav-robotics-mechatronics-drone-prototyping-integration-field-testing-delft-234540","tags":["Internships"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Delft","created_at":1794292815},{"slug":"production-esg-data-engineer-amsterdam-214778","company_name":"ONE-Dyas B.V.","title":"Production & ESG Data Engineer","description":"<p class="MsoNormal">Are you passionate about data, technology and sustainability? ONE-Dyas is looking for a <strong>Production &amp; ESG Data Engineer</strong> to ensure the accurate collection, administration and reporting of production, hydrocarbon and ESG data. You will turn complex data into reliable insights that support operational and business decisions.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>What will you do?</h3><p class="MsoNormal">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Maintain and improve databases containing validated production and ESG data.</p><p class="MsoNormal">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Collect and integrate data from production sources and operated and non-operated assets.</p><p class="MsoNormal">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Prepare clear monthly, quarterly and annual reports and visualizations.</p><p class="MsoNormal">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Support Production, Engineering, HSE and ESG teams with data supporting operational and business decisions.</p><p class="MsoNormal">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Explore opportunities for automation, machine learning and AI to improve collection, administration and reporting.</p> <br> <p class="MsoNormal">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; A bachelor’s level in Engineering, Accounting, Computer Science, Environmental Sciences or a related field.</p><p class="MsoNormal">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience in data engineering or ESG reporting, preferably within the energy or oil &amp; gas industry.</p><p class="MsoNormal">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Knowledge of database management, data visualization and data governance.</p><p class="MsoNormal">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Preferably experience with Python, SQL or similar tools.</p><p class="MsoNormal">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Strong communication and problem-solving skills.</p><p class="MsoNormal">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; A proactive, independent and team-oriented approach with an interest in sustainability.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>Meet ONE-Dyas</h3><p class="MsoNormal">ONE-Dyas B.V. is the largest privately owned exploration and production company in the Netherlands. As entrepreneurs in Dutch offshore gas and oil, the company aims to make a significant contribution to the energy transition, working at the forefront of sustainability and technological innovation. Extracting gas and oil close to home contributes to the national economy, security of supply, and climate goals by employing local services, products, and know-how, reducing the reliance on imported fuels, cutting emissions, and complying to the highest environmental standards in the industry.</p><p class="MsoNormal">With its roots dating back to 1893 in the mining industry, ONE-Dyas has a long history of successfully pioneering energy solutions. Today, its operations span the full lifecycle of offshore assets in the Netherlands, Germany and the UK, including the flagship N05-A development project in the Dutch and German part of the North Sea, set to be the first of its kind to integrate natural gas, wind power and green hydrogen. ONE-Dyas is also actively exploring carbon capture and storage, and green hydrogen opportunities as future energy solutions.</p><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal">Headquartered on the Zuid-as in Amsterdam with around 150 employees, ONE-Dyas has a strong entrepreneurial culture, short lines across all disciplines and a strong relationship with its shareholders leading to a focused and effective work environment. ONE-Dyas has an excellent reputation in the Netherlands, the UK and Germany for its experience and skills across the entire oil &amp; gas energy supply chain. ONE-Dyas is known for getting things done safe, reliably and efficiently.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>Interested?</h3><p class="MsoNormal">Would you like to contribute to reliable production and ESG reporting at ONE-Dyas? We look forward to hearing from you! You can apply for this position via the application form (see link below).</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">If you have any questions about the position, please contact Gerlof Visser (Head of Production Engineering &amp; HCA): <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ----------<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/one-dyas-bv/production-esg-data-engineer-amsterdam-214778","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1794292303},{"slug":"security-engineer-remote-netherlands-471107","company_name":"EverAI","title":"Security Engineer (Remote - Netherlands)","description":"<h1>Our Vision &amp; Products</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>🚀 EverAI — Building the Future of AI Companionship</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>One of the Top 15 Largest &amp; Fastest-Growing AI Companies in the World</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>50 Million Users in 2 years — Help Us Reach 100M first, 500M next</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At <strong>EverAI</strong>, we’re shaping what it means to connect with AI. With <strong>50 million users and counting</strong>, we're not just building products — we're creating entirely new categories.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our flagship product is the <strong>world’s largest AI companionship platform</strong>, redefining relationships for millions. It is governed by our proprietary moderation system, EverGuard — an internal AI designed to ensure everything we build is <strong>safe, ethical, and human-first</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>And we’re only just getting started!</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Our Team</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are an enthusiastic, passionate and hardworking team of ≈ 100 people. Our founding team has strong entrepreneurial experience building and scaling web products from 0 to IPO.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Alexis Soulopoulos </strong>[CEO]</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>• 10+ years in Tech Executive Leadership</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>• Co-Founder Mad Paws Holdings (from 0 to IPO)</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>• Forbes 30 under 30 + Deloitte TechFast50 ’22 &amp; ‘23</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Michael Monin</strong> [Co-founder &amp; CTO]</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>• 10+ years as CTO / COO (web2/web3), 3 years in AI/LLM</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>• Serial-entrepreneur: MTK Digital (exited / 0-&gt;$20m revenue) and Zipchat (AI Chatbot for E-commerce brands)</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Thomas Lacroix </strong>[Co-founder &amp; CMO]</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>• 8+ years in Customer Acquisition &amp; E-commerce Growth</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>• Serial-entrepreneur: Curatible (sold to Blackstone) and MTK Digital (exited / 0-&gt;$20m revenue)</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Maruša Fasano </strong>[CFO/Legal]</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>• 25+ years in Finance, Strategy, M&amp;A</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>• Ex-CFO/M&amp;A @Curatible (exited to Blackstone)</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>• Ex-President of the Board @SotremoSA (exited)</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>• Co-founder/CFO @SoftOne (exited)</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Your Role</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a <strong>Security Engineer</strong>, you’ll own application security for a fast-growing AI companionship platform. This is a hands-on AppSec role: you’ll review code, find real vulnerabilities and drive fixes across the stack. You’ll be the main security person in the company, reporting directly to our CTO and Co-Founder. You’ll set direction yourself and explain risk clearly to non-security colleagues. Our product includes AI-generated content, including NSFW content, and you’ll also keep an eye on AI-specific threats like prompt injection. Real ownership from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This isn’t an infrastructure, networking or DevSecOps role: we’re looking for application security depth.<br /></p><h1><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong><br /></h1><h2><em>Application security (the core of the role)</em></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review code every week to catch vulnerabilities before they ship</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Find, prioritize and drive fixes for real vulnerabilities across the stack, not surface-level issues</p></li></ul><h2><em>Audits and pentests</em></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate external security audits and penetration tests</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Challenge findings where needed, and follow them through to fixes</p></li></ul><h2><em>Engineering and automation</em></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Automate security work and build the tools you need to scale it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use AI tools daily in your security work: code review, pentests and scripting</p></li></ul><h2><em>Ownership and communication</em></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own security end to end with little support, and decide what matters most</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Explain technical risk in plain words to the team and leadership</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cover security alerts, including occasional night and weekend on-call</p></li></ul><h2><em>Also part of the role (lighter)</em></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep a simple risk register and GRC documentation up to date</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share security updates with the team and run awareness training</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Watch emerging AI threats (prompt injection, jailbreaks, content filter bypass) and incidents at our AI providers</p></li></ul><h1>Your Qualifications<br /></h1><h2><strong>Must-haves</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>2+ years</strong> of hands-on security experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands-on AppSec, not compliance only:</strong> you review code regularly and can walk us through a real vulnerability you found and fixed</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Audits and pentests:</strong> you’ve coordinated an external audit or pentest and followed the findings through to fixes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Engineering workflows:</strong> you ship code with Git/GitHub, script in Python or Bash, and have recent hands-on work on a modern web stack (e.g. Rails, Node; GCP, Heroku or similar)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership with little support:</strong> you’ve been the sole or lead security person, or owned a security area on your own. You’ve reviewed code or tested systems every week in the last 2 years, and you explain risk clearly to non-technical people</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI in your daily work:</strong> you use AI tools every day in your security work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A hacker mindset:</strong> You love breaking things to make them safer, and security isn’t only your job: you do it for fun too, through bug bounties, CTFs, research, write-ups or your own tools.</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>Nice-to-haves</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">⭐ <strong>AI/LLM security testing</strong> (prompt injection, jailbreaking): a strong plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience at an AI company or a scale-up</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">GRC awareness</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with MDM and access management</p></li></ul><h1><br /><strong>Soft Skills</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">🗣 Strong communication &amp; collaborative skills (perfectly fluent in English)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🧢 Goal-orientated, ownership and commitment</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">⚡️ Doer mindset - we are moving fast and we need people who can find the right balance between executing, planning and strategy</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🧢 Humble - willing to learn, open to feedback</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🍭 #NSFW - you are comfortable working in an environment with products that are based on uncensored models and content</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Why EverAI?</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">📈 <strong>Exponential Growth</strong>: From 50M users in 2 years, to 100M next — and 500M beyond</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🚀 <strong>Track Record of Category-Creating Innovation</strong>: We consistently launch <strong>world-first AI applications</strong> — setting the pace, not following it</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌍 <strong>Global Impact</strong>: Top-tier user growth, real-world adoption, and cultural relevance</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🧠 <strong>Proven Leadership</strong>: A senior team that’s <strong>launched, scaled, and exited &amp; IPO’d multiple scale ups</strong> — now fully focused on reshaping AI companionship</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">👥 <strong>Elite Remote Team</strong>: 100% remote and built to win — world-class talent from <strong>Tier 1 tech companies</strong>, with a culture of ownership, velocity, and radical creativity</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🛡️ <strong>Ethical Core</strong>: Our AI ecosystem is governed by <strong>EverGuard, our proprietary AI moderation technology</strong>, ensuring responsible development at scale</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>What We Offer</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">✍️ <strong>Contract Type:</strong> We prefer B2B, but we’re flexible, what matters is long-term commitment and impact<br />📍 <strong>Work From Anywhere:</strong> Fully remote. Choose the environment where you do your best work<br />🏝️ <strong>Paid Time Off:</strong> 4 weeks (20 working days) of PTO per year to recharge and reset<br />👨‍👩‍👧‍👦 <strong>Annual Gathering:</strong> A yearly in-person meetup to connect, brainstorm, and celebrate wins together<br />❤️‍🩹 <strong>Health &amp; Wellness Support: </strong>Monthly allowance of<strong> </strong>100 USD for health insurance expenses &amp; access to unlimited 1:1 sessions with psychologists and lifestyle experts through <em>OpenUp </em>(also available to up to three of your family members)<br />🏢 <strong>Co-Working Space Budget:</strong> Work from a co-working space up to twice per month (35 EUR / 40 USD per visit) to stay inspired and connected<br />📚 <strong>Learning Budget:</strong> Dedicated funds to support your professional growth: courses, books, conferences, events, or certifications<br />💻 <strong>Company Laptop &amp; Equipment:</strong> Laptop provided + monitor budget up to 250 USD + keyboard/mouse/mic/headphones budget up to 150 USD<br />⚡ <strong>AI Tools Access:</strong> Premium access to ChatGPT, Hugging Face, Claude Code, and any other tool needed to excel at your job, power your ideas and workflows</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>🎯 Top Tier Talent Is Our Multiplier</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re a fully remote group of <strong>A-players from Tier 1 tech</strong>, led by an exec team who’ve <strong>launched, scaled, and exited multiple companies</strong>. We move fast, and care deeply about what we build — and who we build it with.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for <strong>exceptional talent</strong> ready to ship &amp; distribute world-first AI products at scale, fast, and co-create with us this category-defining business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>If that’s you — reach out and apply!</strong></p><hr><p>Compensation: €65K – €115K • Multiple Ranges</p><ul><li>Mid • Annual Compensation Range (Gross) €65K – €85K</li><li>Senior • Annual Compensation Range (Gross) €85K – €115K</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/everai/security-engineer-remote-netherlands-471107","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Netherlands","created_at":1794282015},{"slug":"stage-bouw-hengelo-458409","company_name":"Dura Vermeer","title":"Stage Bouw","description":"<p><em><span style="color:#121317">Hé stage topper! Kom jij, net als vele andere stagiaires, stagelopen bij Dura Vermeer Bouw en Vastgoed Hengelo? Bij ons krijg jij de kans om mee te denken, werken én ontwikkelen aan gave projecten binnen Noord, Midden en Oost-Nederland. Wij hebben weer volop stageplekken vanaf </span></em><strong><em><span style="color:#121317">Februari 2027</span></em></strong><em><span style="color:#121317"> op onze bouwen en op kantoor! </span></em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Dit wordt jouw stage</span></strong></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">Als stagiair bij Dura Vermeer Bouw en Vastgoed Hengelo ga je aan de slag op ons kantoor of op één van onze projecten. We kijken in overeenstemming welke afdeling of welk project het beste bij jou en/of de opdracht past. Tijdens je stage word je goed begeleid door één van onze collega’s en krijg je de ruimte om jezelf verder te ontwikkelen!  Jij staat aan het stuur van je eigen ontwikkeling tijdens je stageperiode: Hoe meer jij wil leren, hoe meer jij kan leren! Naast dat je zelfstandig aan een opdracht kan werken wordt je ook begeleidt door een senior collega die jou alle kneepjes van het vak gaat leren. We hebben door heel ons werkgebied verschillende bouwen waar we ruimte hebben voor een stagiaire, stuur ons vooral een berichtje zodat we samen kunnen kijken wat passend is!</span></p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Meer bij Dura Vermeer</span></strong></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">Dura Vermeer is een familiebedrijf. Een onafhankelijke bouwonderneming actief in woningbouw, utiliteitsbouw, infrastructuur en techniek in Nederland. Al sinds 1855 vormen onze onafhankelijkheid en langjarige continuïteit de basis voor onze strategie. Met een omzet van circa € 1,8 miljard en ruim 3.000 medewerkers behoren we tot de top van de Nederlandse bouwsector. Samen realiseren we prachtige projecten. Iconische, en soms ook alledaagse projecten waarmee we nieuwe antwoorden bieden op maatschappelijke vraagstukken. Waarmee we de beste oplossingen voor morgen garanderen en het verschil maken voor Nederland, juist op de langere termijn. We hebben stevige ambities – en daarvoor geldt dat we die alleen kunnen waarmaken dankzij onze mensen. 