<p>As a Senior Product Marketing Manager, you will take full ownership of product marketing strategy in a fast-growing, international AdTech environment. You will shape how innovative advertising technology products are positioned, communicated, and brought to market. Working closely with product, sales, customer success, and other cross-functional teams, you will translate complex technical capabilities into compelling value propositions. You will play a key role in developing go-to-market strategies, enabling commercial teams, and strengthening customer engagement. By combining market intelligence, customer insights, and data-driven storytelling, you will help drive business growth and product adoption. This is an opportunity to join a collaborative, remote-first team and contribute to the evolution of programmatic advertising across mobile and connected TV.</p>
</div><br><strong>Accountabilities</strong><br><div>
<p data-pm-slice="1 3 []">You will lead product marketing initiatives from strategy development to execution, ensuring consistent positioning and effective communication across customer-facing teams.</p>
<ul data-spread="false">
<li>
<p>Develop and execute product marketing strategies to promote products and solutions to existing and prospective B2B customers.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Create compelling marketing content and bold narratives that clearly communicate product value, differentiation, and competitive advantages.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Collaborate closely with product teams to ensure marketing messaging accurately reflects product features, capabilities, and developments.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Lead go-to-market initiatives for new product launches and equip sales and customer success teams with effective messaging and enablement materials.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Engage regularly with customers and internal stakeholders to collect feedback, understand market needs, and identify emerging industry trends.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Partner with sales and customer success teams to align marketing execution with business objectives and customer insights.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Monitor campaign and product marketing performance against key performance indicators, using data to identify opportunities for improvement.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Leverage MarTech platforms and AI-powered tools to streamline content creation, improve reporting, optimize segmentation, and deliver personalized marketing experiences.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Anticipate market developments and emerging advertising trends, translating them into relevant product positioning and forward-looking marketing narratives.</p>
</li>

<p><strong>Requirements</strong>:</p>
<p>You are a proactive and strategic marketing professional with strong expertise in B2B advertising technology, excellent communication skills, and the ability to influence teams across a dynamic international organization.</p>
<ul data-spread="false">
<li>
<p>At least 5 years of experience in B2B AdTech, ideally within a startup or scaleup environment, with a proven track record in product marketing.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Strong understanding of the programmatic advertising ecosystem, particularly mobile advertising trends, challenges, and opportunities.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Solid knowledge of AI tools and demonstrated ability to integrate them into everyday marketing workflows.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Experience with marketing platforms and tools such as HubSpot and WordPress is a plus.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Excellent writing and editing skills, with the ability to develop engaging stories and compelling messaging for B2B audiences.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Strong analytical skills and the ability to translate complex data and insights into differentiated marketing narratives.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Excellent command of English, both written and spoken.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously and adapt quickly to changing priorities.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Outstanding organizational skills and meticulous attention to detail.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Genuine passion for mobile marketing and app advertising, with a strong interest in emerging technologies and industry developments.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Comfortable working in a fast-paced, dynamic, remote-first, and international environment.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Proven ability to collaborate with and influence cross-functional teams without formal authority, particularly across sales, customer success, and product management.</p>
</li>

<p><strong>Benefits</strong>:</p>
<ul data-spread="false">
<li>
<p>Exceptional opportunities for career growth and professional development.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The opportunity to work alongside experienced industry experts and entrepreneurs shaping the future of AdTech.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Direct, day-to-day collaboration with the leadership team.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>A fun, ambitious, and multinational team distributed across Europe, India, Argentina, and soon the United States.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Flexible work-from-home arrangements.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>A $500 home-office setup budget.</p>
